{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries","id":292532,"title":"[Open Development] Ordo Dracul Merits and Mysteries","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-25T17:24:14-07:00","id":292532,"title":"[Open Development] Ordo Dracul Merits and Mysteries","content":"The Ordo Dracul open dev public document is available.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries-the-rites-of-the-dragon-vampire-the-requiem/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries-the-rites-of-the-dragon-vampire-the-requiem/\" target=\"_blank\"> Ordo Dracul Merits and Mysteries: The Rites of the Dragon [Vampire: The Requiem] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries-the-rites-of-the-dragon-vampire-the-requiem/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries-the-rites-of-the-dragon-vampire-the-requiem/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T17:42:07-07:00","id":292551,"title":"","content":"<u>Rites of the Impaled</u>: Love this fighting style. I love it to pieces. Beyond the Pale is exactly the sort of thing I was hoping to see for the Impaled. Two thumbs up.<br /> <br /> <u>Twilight Judge</u>: The Sworn of the Dying Light are my personal favorite, and this merit is very, very cool. It seems like it might be a little <i>too</i> cool, but only if you have a consensus among Judges in a domain if you get crazy with your rulings. Perhaps some kind of limit on the heresy exceptions a judge can impose (don't have a solid suggestion at this point, just a thought) wouldn't go amiss.<br /> <br /> <u>Wyrm's Nest Merits</u>: I'm including Nest Guardian in this. In general these are fantastic, and Nests really needed some solid, non-crazy optional rule support.<br /> <br /> Chapterhouse is nice.<br /> <br /> Crucible might benefit from some discussion of how long you have to spend studying within it to reap the benefit. &quot;I'll swing by the Crucible right before I spend my experience!&quot;<br /> <br /> The reference to &quot;ectoplasmic energies&quot; in Occult Alignment is a little ghost-centric, perhaps that wording can be changed to something more general?<br /> <br /> The Mysteries are going to require a little bit more chewing when I have some quiet time, but in the broad strokes I'm intrigued. The Coil of Ziva is tripping me up a little with Siphon the Soul, seems like the theme of the Mystery takes a hard left, but perhaps the 3 dot Coil would help bridge that gap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","user":"Smarmy Vamp","date":". 11-03-2014, 07:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T17:52:25-07:00","id":292556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=292551#post292551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Rites of the Impaled</u>: The Coil of Ziva is tripping me up a little with Siphon the Soul, seems like the theme of the Mystery takes a hard left, but perhaps the 3 dot Coil would help bridge that gap.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I don't think Siphon the Soul meshes well with the other dots and the theme of the makes Coil, it actually makes you roll for detachment, for a Mystery centred on recovering Humanity is kind against it's theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T17:58:51-07:00","id":292559,"title":"","content":"Well, the fact that you can burn Vitae to boost your detachment roll is nice. It's just odd that a Coil about clinging to Humanity gives you a diablerie lite power. Technically it helps hold on to Humanity... sorta... if it all goes well and you don't get axe-murdered for being Tainted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","user":"Smarmy Vamp","date":". 10-25-2014, 09:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T18:17:48-07:00","id":292570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=292559#post292559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the fact that you can burn Vitae to boost your detachment roll is nice. It's just odd that a Coil about clinging to Humanity gives you a diablerie lite power. Technically it helps hold on to Humanity... sorta... if it all goes well and you don't get axe-murdered for being Tainted.</div> </div> </div> </div>A more suiting power would be perhaps that you can choose one Humanity breaking point per dot in the Coil to not risk detachment, kind a reversing of the bane effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T18:26:16-07:00","id":292573,"title":"","content":"What happens when two Twilight Judges disagree?<br /> If a Vampire uses Laying On Hands to cure a disease, are they affected by getting a minor version of an illness they would normally be immune to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 10-25-2014, 09:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T18:40:07-07:00","id":292577,"title":"","content":"Shouldn't the Sworn merit also be the prerequisites for the token Axe Sworn and Dying Light merits? Also where is the token Oath of Mysteries merit. But instead of the already overused access to social merits that's thrown out for everyone maybe give them a merit ability to enable them to glean something from their experience in extended torpor or day sleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","user":"Audrey St. John","date":". 10-27-2014, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T18:44:20-07:00","id":292581,"title":"","content":"I like that wyrm's nests are being treated a little differently, and made into something the Ordo can actually be considered to -hold- now, instead of the BS about the Ordo not being able to reliably keep them. I do think that Occult Alignment should focus on attributes instead of skills, though, as skills seem a bit underpowered.<br /> <br /> I do wish there were some more nest merits, though, and while fontal rituals always sucked, I'd love for there to be something similarly 'open ended', that is, you learn it and can then, say, create specific rituals/experiments at individual nests.<br /> <br /> The Mystery of Zirnitra is awesome, and a lot like a 1st edition coil I statted out once, which gave you unseen sense and then eventually other mortal-only things like second sight powers and whatever else. Really glad to see something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T18:51:47-07:00","id":292585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=292573#post292573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens when two Twilight Judges disagree?<br /> If a Vampire uses Laying On Hands to cure a disease, are they affected by getting a minor version of an illness they would normally be immune to?</div> </div> </div> </div>They don their powdered wigs and fight to the death. Occasionally someone shouts out &quot;OBJECTION!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T19:03:30-07:00","id":292594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=292585#post292585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don their powdered wigs and fight to the death. Occasionally someone shouts out &quot;OBJECTION!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://objection.mrdictionary.net/go.php?n=7611342\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://objection.mrdictionary.net/go.php?n=7611342\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://objection.mrdictionary.net/go.php?n=7611342\" target=\"_blank\"> http://objection.mrdictionary.net/go.php?n=7611342 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T19:05:19-07:00","id":292597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=292594#post292594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"http://objection.mrdictionary.net/go.php?n=7611342\" target=\"_blank\">http://objection.mrdictionary.net/go.php?n=7611342</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly that!<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh Dear. Dave, you have introduced me to a <i>terrible</i> thing.<br /> <br /> EDIT: So, onto the actual material:<br /> <br /> Nothing immediately stands out as problematic to me. Second Sight fans will be able to tap into a low end image of the hermetic vampire of the old Tremere. I like the Impaled Fighting Style-I love sheer tough it out and dish it out types as much as I do dodge and flow with everything types. Dragon's Nest Merits make the nests feel more...quarantined, which is not a bad feel for the occult scientists. Twilight Judge filled me with stories. THe first set of coils and scales are, of course, some thing of the big, new add, and I question how much the Ordo would actually devalue it-it certainly ties into the idea of becoming the better class of monster, ascending sideways as it were. On top of that, while not as potent as other powers, supernatural merits are just damn useful. The second set of coils and scales, on the other hand, is wonderfully heretical to their thinking, and on a different front a nifty parallel to the Ascending Ones's elixir that allows them to become a vampire for a while(Hooray kinship! Hooray for the Cult of Set!).<br /> <br /> My only objection,at this point, is the naming. I mean, they're cool? And I'm sure practice makes perfect? But those are some tough names.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-25-2014, 10:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T19:43:17-07:00","id":292602,"title":"","content":"The cure disease effect of lay on hands requiring multiple successes goes against the general rules for instant actions. That should really be a dice penalty instead of a target number of successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T20:00:35-07:00","id":292616,"title":"","content":"I really love the idea of a coil that lets a vampire take human-only Supernal merits, but I'm also really worried about its potential for abuse, since obviously every human Merit won't be screened for &quot;will this break the game if a Vampire takes it?&quot; Off the top of my head, this allows two Vampires to take the Producer Merit and get unlimited Vitae from each other. Ironically, it was made human-only instead of human or ghoul during development, specifically to avoid that sort of abuse","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T20:05:21-07:00","id":292618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=292616#post292616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really love the idea of a coil that lets a vampire take human-only Supernal merits, but I'm also really worried about its potential for abuse, since obviously every human Merit won't be screened for &quot;will this break the game if a Vampire takes it?&quot; Off the top of my head, this allows two Vampires to take the Producer Merit and get unlimited Vitae from each other. Ironically, it was made human-only instead of human or ghoul during development, specifically to avoid that sort of abuse</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one of those things where I think common sense saves the day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-26-2014, 12:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T20:07:55-07:00","id":292619,"title":"","content":"I agree that Siphon Soul seems like an odd choice for a Coil. It would make more sense to me as a Scale. I know that the Mystery is considered heretical anyway, but it seems antithetical to have pseudo-Amaranth as a mainstream line of research for the Mystery that mostly appeals to vampires trying to become more human. I'd also prefer if there was a requirement that the victim's Humanity was higher than the Dragon's. It evokes the idea that pure souls are more valuable. Also, could the Dragon use a Bane to negate the Detachment roll, or is it unavoidable like regular Amaranth?<br /> <br /> Does Numbing Touch break the Willpower per turn limit? The way I read the second paragraph, the &quot;psychic weapon&quot; version of the power costs two Willpower: one when the power is first used and another when it hits the target. Is this version meant to take two rounds to perform? If so, it probably should be clarified. If I am misreading it, well either I'm dense or it still needs to be clarified. Both are likely.<br /> <br /> Edited to Add: Wouldn't the easiest fix to balance the Producer merit for Ghouls be to add a drawback that, since their blood is more potent, healing damage from feeding takes 2 Vitae per lethal damage? Keeping track of damage caused by feeding doesn't seem any worse than having to track damage related to various tilts. Besides, feeding damage is already &quot;sort of&quot; tracked to determine when the Drained Condition is applied.<br /> <br /> Edit 2: Weird secondary point... Producer by RAW only deals with Vitae gained from inflicting lethal damage during a feeding. Kindred would probably get zero benefit from taking the merit even if it was allowed. I doubt that RAI would be any more generous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3755,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","user":"Jaerys","date":". 10-25-2014, 11:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T20:35:43-07:00","id":292631,"title":"","content":"NEW COILS YES!<br /> <br /> Oh, and Merits. Those are nice too, I guess.<br /> <br /> BUT MYSTERIES AND COILS AND <i>SCALES</i>!<br /> <br /> EDIT: The Coil of Zirnitra is <i>love</i>. I would still purchase the book even if there was nothing else for the Ordo but that Coil. But I am glad that there will be <i>so much more.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T20:38:40-07:00","id":292632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=292618#post292618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's one of those where I think common sense saves the day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, for sure. Especially since it's a &quot;rare&quot; Coil, chances are if you're taking it, you're already working closely with your ST to work out the details, so I doubt it will be a big issue. Just giving an obligatory &quot;hey, this is easily broken if you combine it with this other power&quot; comment for diligence's sake.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jaerys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=292619#post292619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit 2: Weird secondary point... Producer by RAW only deals with Vitae gained from inflicting lethal damage during a feeding. Kindred would probably get zero benefit from taking the merit even if it was allowed. I doubt that RAI would be any more generous.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's also a good point. I wasn't so much concerned with Producer specifically as I was using it as an example of how allowing vampires to take Merits vampires aren't supposed to be able to have is clearly asking for trouble. I don't think there's any way for such a power not to be abusable, but if there's any spare wordcount (haha... yeah, probably not...) a sidebar or something just reminding ST's that it's highly abuseable and to use their best judgement would be nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-25-2014, 11:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T20:47:39-07:00","id":292646,"title":"","content":"For the most part, I like the merits presented here. The fighting style (rights of the impaled) stands out as the best presented, but I agree with Audrey that being sworn should be a prerequisite for this merit as well as twilight judge. Further, where is the love for sworn of the mysteries? We need some political merits please.<br /> <br /> As for the Mysteries: well, I can't find anything within them that interests me. The first one, Zirnitra just doesn't fit with the order to me, as it is really just an excuse to turn another covenant into mages. My recomendation is to scrap this coil and go back to the drawing board.<br /> <br /> As for the Coil of Ziva, I like the theme, but not the execution. The first two dots are pretty good, but the last two I really don't like. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> How about some thing like this:<br /> <br /> Third Tier: Enliven the Heart<br /> The character can experience the full range of human emotions. This inner core of emotion fortifies the Dragon against conditions that threaten their Soul. The character is immune to the effects of the Jaded, Soulless, and Tainted Conditions.<br /> <br /> or maybe:<br /> Third Tier: Enliven the Soul (this one is a slightly modified version of coil of the locust from the Ordo Covenant book.)<br /> The character's aura becomes as vivid as that of a mortal. They do not suffer breaking points from events related to kindred milestones or from lack of interaction with mortals. Further, the Dragon is not subject to the affects of the Predatory Aura, nor does he provoke it in others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T20:49:19-07:00","id":292647,"title":"","content":"To be entirely fair, I don't think the coil itself would be a problem; I know that I would probably end up banning or houseruling Grafting Unholy Flesh before touching the rest of the Coil itself.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, someone asking me whether they could take Producer would get a small smile and a &quot;Producer isn't a Supernatural Merit in my games, just a medical condition. Why not take City Walking or Clairvoyance or something?&quot;<br /> <br /> EDIT: Wait, how do stuff like Psychokinesis work with the &quot;Drawback triggers all the time&quot;? Psychokinesis and Telekinesis just activate when you run out of Willpower without any control on your part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 10-25-2014, 11:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T21:01:33-07:00","id":292648,"title":"","content":"I think the intention is that the drawbacks always trigger regardless of success or failure rule is supposed to only apply to drawbacks that trigger on failures. Drawbacks for things like Psychokinesis and Telekinesis should work normally. It could benefit from some clarification though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T21:03:52-07:00","id":292649,"title":"","content":"I honestly think this book was something the Ordo Dracul greatly needed. They always felt a little constrained compared to the other Covenants especially due to the rapidly increasing cost of coils. This book so far seems to fill in a lot of the gaps in abilities that help make Ordo Dracul the go to covenant for Kindred who wish to improve themselves of their condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T22:09:30-07:00","id":292684,"title":"","content":"Wait, wait, wait, rewind.<br /> <br /> Does the Mystery of Zirnitra allow you to, essentially, play a wolf-blooded vampire?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T22:14:10-07:00","id":292685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=292684#post292684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, wait, wait, rewind.<br /> <br /> Does the Mystery of Zirnitra allow you to, essentially, play a wolf-blooded vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no, not again!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T22:19:34-07:00","id":292699,"title":"","content":"They specifically call out Wolf-Blooded seeking to reclaim some of their supernatural power from prior to being a Vampire in the article. Look forward to Wolf-Blooded Tells from Werewolf Second Edition!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T22:23:02-07:00","id":292701,"title":"","content":"What. What have you done.<br /> <br /> I leave for a few months and this is what I come back to.<br /> <br /> What the hell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T22:24:22-07:00","id":292702,"title":"","content":"#turneverythreadintoanidigamthread<br /> <br /> But that aside, What's up Charly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T22:25:52-07:00","id":292705,"title":"","content":"Ooh, yeah, that might be problematic.<br /> <br /> However, we don't know how Wolf-Blooded will work, not exactly. For all we know, it could be referring to recovering stuff like Lunatic Glare, rather than stuff like Tells.<br /> <br /> EDIT: You know what I'M looking forward to? Endowments.<br /> <br /> I'm holding out for Castigation, thank you very much. Or Rites of Denial. Those'd be nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 10-26-2014, 01:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T22:29:50-07:00","id":292721,"title":"","content":"I loved the hell out of Blood and Smoke's Ordo Dracul because now it had both the awesome fluff and solid mechanics representing their quest for improvement with solid, entertaining and intriguingly-designed mechanics.<br /> <br /> This is full gonzo. This is discarding the latter part and going with a philosophy of &quot;sounds cool, throw it in.&quot; <br /> <br /> Cross-splat powers? Really? Have we learned nothing from a decade in this business?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T22:38:29-07:00","id":292728,"title":"","content":"If that's what it takes to get you back in regular involvement with the WoD Forums, Omi, I'll take it. We really don't see you here enough.<br /> <br /> But that aside, I think there's some decent testing of the water to be done.<br /> <br /> Very, <i>very</i> careful testing of the water.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T23:10:17-07:00","id":292750,"title":"","content":"As someone who actually rather likes the Coil of Zinatra (I was joking about the Endowments), I would say that it'll probably be fine, as long as Grafting Unholy Flesh doesn't show up in the book.<br /> <br /> Because Grafting Unholy Flesh is <i>broken</i>. In the &quot;I'm going to just go ahead and steal this Demon's immunity to lie detection&quot; sense.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, the Coil will be fine,as long as the pool of Merits is limited; it requires a high amount of dialogue with your ST*, but I'm OK with that.<br /> <br /> I also see no conflict between the goal of the Mystery and that of the Ordo - it makes a certain amount of sense to me, and not in a gonzo way.<br /> <br /> * Check out the back of B&amp;S. Notice that none of the Merits are explicitly marked as Supernatural merits. As of <i>right now</i>, the only Merits this explicitly empowers our Ordo member to pick up are those under the &quot;Supernatural&quot; section in the GMC appendix and the ones under the Coil in the doc. Anything more is your ST being nice to you.<br /> <br /> Unless, of course, Flowers of Hell marked some more as explicitly Supernatural; I've not read it yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T23:15:30-07:00","id":292751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=292728#post292728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that's what it takes to get you back in regular involvement with the WoD Forums, Omi, I'll take it. We really don't see you here enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have been<i> told things</i> about Changeling. I dread to look! Where should I head to next?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T23:21:45-07:00","id":292755,"title":"","content":"Look for the Open Development Threads in the Changeling Forum.<br /> <br /> The things you have heard are <i>good things</i> waiting to meet you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T23:24:36-07:00","id":292758,"title":"","content":"I would mandate that lesser template merits like Wolf-Blood or some of the Heir's stuff requires it to be in your backstory, all terrible hooks included(Like, say, the Heir's Cipher)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T23:49:06-07:00","id":292763,"title":"","content":"I don't think this is intended to give you anything but what mortals alone can access, so I very much doubt that Wolf-Blooded merits will be an option.<br /> <br /> What I do think is that all of the thaumaturgy merits from Second Sight will be available, which really allows the Ordo Dracul do some low key ceremonial magic, voodoo, and (non coil) alchemy. Since they're often referenced as sorcerers as well as scientists, this pleases me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T23:55:35-07:00","id":292766,"title":"","content":"Looking around, it looks like the only GMC-era Merits outside of the GMC appendix would be Automatic Writing, Laying On Hands, Numbing Touch, (maybe) Clear Sighted, and (maybe) Producer.<br /> <br /> Of those 5, Producer is pretty much the only one I would disallow (because Hungarian marriages); Clear Sighted could even be thematic.<br /> <br /> I mean, going back to my earlier joke, Endowments are <i>technically</i> available, but they always have been - most kinds of Endowments mention how it is possible for outsiders to steal them, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T00:08:53-07:00","id":292768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=292763#post292763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think this is intended to give you anything but what mortals alone can access, so I very much doubt that Wolf-Blooded merits will be an option.<br /> <br /> What I do think is that all of the thaumaturgy merits from Second Sight will be available, which really allows the Ordo Dracul do some low key ceremonial magic, voodoo, and (non coil) alchemy. Since they're often referenced as sorcerers as well as scientists, this pleases me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd agree with you, but the fluff specifically mentions &quot;Some Dragons have developed this Coil to regain the lost gifts granted to them as part of a werewolf family.&quot; It's possible it's just a reference to the Grafting Unholy Flesh Scale, but it seems a bit misleading if it is just that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T00:44:05-07:00","id":292782,"title":"","content":"I don't have B&amp;S or VtR right at hand, but am I reading the Mortal supernatural merit <i>Automatic Writing</i> right? I thought the Ordo Dracul seriously frown upon letting someone else's spirit overtake your own, as in possession and such; Would the spirit entering the character for the writing count as violating that principle?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T03:28:50-07:00","id":292844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zsander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=292782#post292782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have B&amp;S or VtR right at hand, but am I reading the Mortal supernatural merit <i>Automatic Writing</i> right? I thought the Ordo Dracul seriously frown upon letting someone else's spirit overtake your own, as in possession and such; Would the spirit entering the character for the writing count as violating that principle?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the old version they did and the sentence was final death by sanctioned diablerie. But this is second edition and none of that applies anymore. Besides, you can just take the Twilight Judge merit yourself or bitch slap the Twilight Judge with Majesty or Dominate to authorize you to have the merit. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T03:57:14-07:00","id":292847,"title":"","content":"I gotta say I really like the Coil of Zirnitra as it allows for interesting things, including the possibility implied by the fluff of regaining some of your heritage lost to the Embrace whether that be from being Wolf-Blooded or something else. I also happen to like Grafting the Unholy Flesh though I would not read the Scale allowing for the theft of innate qualities like the Demons ability to Lie perfectly but rather something like a single Embed or a Discipline power etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T05:41:23-07:00","id":292901,"title":"","content":"I'd rule that vampires cannot steal innate parts of a template (unless it directly corresponds with a stealable part of the body). I would allow a vampire to steal demonic form powers though, especially as it is already possible in Demon itself, through demonic form gadgets.<br /> <br /> About Crucible, why don't all Ordo Dracul learn their coils in a Crucible ritual? You could always exchange favors to get access to someone elses. Doesn't this in practice make the learning of Ordo powers cheaper for all members? I also don't like that it creates discrepancies in power, even if characters have the same amounts of XP. I like to keep XP costs as a meta thing, and if it changes I would like it to change retroactively. But I understand how this doens't work for such a merit.<br /> <br /> About Independent Study, it seems obvious that exchanging this merit for status 2 in the Ordo happens instead of the Sancticity of Merits rule kicking in, but it isn't said explicitly. Under strict reading, one could argue that first you lose the merit, getting 2 XP back through Sancticity of Merits, and then get Status 2 for free. But does doesn't seem te be the intention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T05:45:15-07:00","id":292905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Audrey St. John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=292844#post292844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the old version they did and the sentence was final death by sanctioned diablerie. But this is second edition and none of that applies anymore. Besides, you can just take the Twilight Judge merit yourself or bitch slap the Twilight Judge with Majesty or Dominate to authorize you to have the merit.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Automatic Writing would certainly be cause for concern, and observation by the Twilight Sworn. The prohibition is against losing your will to outside forces. Automatic Writing, when it works the way you want it to, doesn't stray into prohibited territory, but it's close. A Dragon who uses the merit often and is constantly haunted, or becomes dependent on the outside insight rather than developing his own has become a problem.<br /> <br /> Also... why exactly does none of that apply anymore? The Covenant books are still relevant in the broad strokes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T07:20:01-07:00","id":292956,"title":"","content":"No the prohibition is against willfully ceding control of soul (such as it is) to other entities for power or esoteric knowledge, which is exactly what you are doing when you permit a ghost, demon, angel etc. to use your body to scrawl messages. <br /> Involuntarily losing control would be problematic and quickly reduce the covenant to non existence if there was any attempt at enforcement since there's always been Dominate, and, if you're going by several of the noisier forumites' interpretation, Majesty is both unresistable and undetectable. <br /> <br /> As for why much of the Ordo Dracul covenant book doesn't apply anymore. How about by pointing out that their purpose isn't transcending the vampiric curse, but spitting on God and that Dracula is not their founder. Then there's a bunch of other little things like how knowledge of the Coils or belonging to a Greater Oath does not denote covenant rank any longer. Or how Kogaion went from being a singular individual who knew of all the wyrm's nest in a domain and advisor to the Oath Sworn to a singular undisputed leader of the covenant, not the Oath Sworn. While I never particularly cared overmuch for the concept of the Mysteries Sworn, (I find it unlikely that more than one or two would actually exist in most domains given their stringent requirements.) with the emphasis on drinking Vitae to accomplish anything, they're even less relevant now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","user":"Audrey St. John","date":". 10-27-2014, 10:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T07:32:06-07:00","id":292961,"title":"","content":"Passing through Pain: What the heck is a relevant dice pool? Do you mean &quot;any dice pool that would normally have suffered from the wound penalty?&quot;<br /> <br /> Anyone else think that Twilight Judge ought to have a higher status requirement? They can basically make pope like decrees, but I'm pretty sure that the pope would have catholic church status 5 as a requirement. <br /> <br /> Grafting Unholy flesh, was the intent for the dragon to gain extra organs, or to replace body parts with replacements, or both? Having a magic power through a mismatched eye is different from having a magic power thanks to a third eye in the forehead which is different from a dragon having three powers by replacing both eyes and adding a third one to the forehead.....<br /> <br /> I presume that the piece of brain removed in a psychic lobotomy would automatically be a valid implant for grafting unholy flesh? <br /> <br /> As for the coils of ziva, I think the fluff and the rules are as mismatched as the children of osiris in owod, who were supposed to be unliving saints but had a discipline that allowed them to retain their humanity no matter how mind bogglingly horrific their actions. Siphon the soul allows them to diablorize without humanity going down for example.<br /> <br /> I suggest making it either a coil about being as horrific a monster as one can imagine thanks to protection against humanity loss or make it a coil about being more mortal, not both which is really weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T07:38:12-07:00","id":292967,"title":"","content":"Dominate and Majesty have nothing to do with this issue, I'm talking about being overtaken by otherworldly spirits, demons, etc. There's an entire bloodline that revolves around controlling, utilizing, and eating ghosts. Automatic Writing makes delightful amounts of sense for them, and if it gets out of hand they just devour the troublesome shade and move on. Unless the ghost gets its hooks into the Dragolescu's soul, then it becomes a problem.<br /> <br /> As for the rest of what you wrote... I can't meaningfully respond to that without hijacking the thread.<br /> <br /> There are a lot of strange assertions floating around in this thread that are perplexing to me. There was talk earlier about the Impaled being part of the Axe Sworn. That's just not the case. There's some overlap because the Rites of the Impaled are very martial, but there's no requirement for an Impaled to be Sworn of the Axe. They're kind of a cult within a cult.<br /> <br /> <u>Grafting Unholy Flesh:</u> There's some serious potential for crazyness here, but it's mitigated by the fact that you have to hunt and restrain whatever it is you want to steal from. That's not exactly trivial most of the time and comes with enough peril that I think it's okay at its base. Can you cut multiple bits out of the same creature to take multiple powers from it? I echo the suggestion that's come up that there should be some clarity as to what you can take (innate traits vs. dot powers). Can you have as many powers grafted in as you can get bits?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T07:58:02-07:00","id":292974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=292901#post292901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About Crucible, why don't all Ordo Dracul learn their coils in a Crucible ritual? You could always exchange favors to get access to someone elses. Doesn't this in practice make the learning of Ordo powers cheaper for all members? I also don't like that it creates discrepancies in power, even if characters have the same amounts of XP. I like to keep XP costs as a meta thing, and if it changes I would like it to change retroactively. But I understand how this doens't work for such a merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel much the same way. Maybe it should be something like a Crucible attunement, where you need the merit to actually benefit from the crucible ritual, this could make viable the retroactive effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2213-tittopaolo210","name":"TittoPaolo210","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T08:06:10-07:00","id":292976,"title":"","content":"Well, I like the idea that you can use your Crucible as a favor or currency. Or PCs without a Crucible can get access to one as part of a story on a one-time basis. Maybe it could work something like Altar, where if you contribute at least a dot you can use it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T09:02:29-07:00","id":292991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=292976#post292976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I like the idea that you can use your Crucible as a favor or currency. Or PCs without a Crucible can get access to one as part of a story on a one-time basis. Maybe it could work something like Altar, where if you contribute at least a dot you can use it?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a really good idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T09:48:13-07:00","id":293003,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Sans\">I don`t realy like Crucible if you have 4+ coil dots or scales there is no reason not the take it<br /> I rather had it work by giving beats that can only be spend on coils and scales<br /> for performing certain procedures on the crucible <br /> <br /> also while I love the idea of Zirnitra I don`t realy like the execution<br /> especialy the 4th and 5th dot<br /> you would expect more from the top powers than some dice modifiers<br /> maybe something like the ability to get devotions which have you supernatural merits as prerequisite <br /> so you get to mix vampiric powers with sorcery and psychic powers</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3902-yao","name":"Yao","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T10:13:25-07:00","id":293028,"title":"","content":"Is it just me or the 5th level of the Coil of Ziva is absurdly strong flavour-wise but really weak mechanically? Am i missing something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2213-tittopaolo210","name":"TittoPaolo210","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T10:23:46-07:00","id":293031,"title":"","content":"Assuming Producer is supernatural, vampires don't produce blood or Vitae so logically the only possible effect would be a vampire can drain the Producer twice as fast. I would limit it to merits that cover actual powers rather than states of being. The Coil seems to provide some states of being when they are prerequisites. Scales should be made to cover any other states of being, fast healing etc.<br /> <br /> I'm surprised nobody mentioned a vampire controlling/creating fire as a problem. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T10:33:09-07:00","id":293056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=293031#post293031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm surprised nobody mentioned a vampire controlling/creating fire as a problem. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that being able to produce/create doesn't make you immune to frenzy or fire damage, and that would be even more dangerous for the vampire itself, since it's really likely that he loses control in the process of creating fire and burn everything (himself included) in the process, if he can bring himself to create fire in the first place and not chicken out a the last moment <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2213-tittopaolo210","name":"TittoPaolo210","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T10:37:35-07:00","id":293058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=293031#post293031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming Producer is supernatural, vampires don't produce blood or Vitae so logically the only possible effect would be a vampire can drain the Producer twice as fast. I would limit it to merits that cover actual powers rather than states of being. The Coil seems to provide some states of being when they are prerequisites. Scales should be made to cover any other states of being, fast healing etc.<br /> <br /> I'm surprised nobody mentioned a vampire controlling/creating fire as a problem. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm not sure Producer even qualifies, and obviously no ST in their right mind would allow Hungarian Marriages that way. But there are plenty of other examples where giving vampires powers that were not made with Requiem in mind could cause problems. As long as that's a known issue, it can be solved with simple common sense and ST discretion. A simple word of caution to STs would alleviate my concerns, personally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T11:12:03-07:00","id":293070,"title":"","content":"How does <i>Denying the Bane</i> (Coil of Ziva 1) interact with Clan Banes exactly? There's no sensible way to apply it to the Ventrue Clan Bane, but what about the others? Nosferatu normally treat there Humanity as 2 lower for social penalties when dealing with humans. Does the Coil negate some of those penalties (in which case that particular benefit caps out at 2 dots)? If so, do Mekhet practitioners of the Coil double dip? Do they both negate the -1 penalty from the Clan Bane and add their full dots in the Coil to their Humanity to the actual Bane calculation? If the Dragon learns the Coil before their Humanity drops to 6, does it prevent the Clan Bane from manifesting until their Humanity is 6 - (dots in the Coil)? It's unlikely, but I could see someone trying to spin it that way.<br /> <br /> I assume it has no impact on the &quot;great bane&quot; of sunlight, or else it's stepping on the Ascendant's toes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3755,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","user":"Jaerys","date":". 10-26-2014, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T11:14:50-07:00","id":293071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TittoPaolo210</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=293056#post293056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that being able to produce/create doesn't make you immune to frenzy or fire damage, and that would be even more dangerous for the vampire itself, since it's really likely that he loses control in the process of creating fire and burn everything (himself included) in the process, if he can bring himself to create fire in the first place and not chicken out a the last moment <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not an issue whatsoever, since anyone wanting to abuse it would also take Coil of Ascendant which gives immunity to fire frenzy.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, one of my players is going for the custom homemade coil of eating spirits (PenDragon's work). With plans to eat fire spirits for some fire powers. And yeah, even before that, he took Coil of Ascendant just to go around the whole frenzy business.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":294,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","user":"Griautis","date":". 10-26-2014, 02:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T11:21:13-07:00","id":293075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jaerys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=293070#post293070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does <i>Denying the Bane</i> (Coil of Ziva 1) interact with Clan Banes exactly? There's no sensible way to apply it to the Ventrue Clan Bane, but what about the others? Nosferatu normally treat there Humanity as 2 lower for social penalties when dealing with humans. Does the Coil negate some of those penalties (in which case that particular benefit caps out at 2 dots)? If so, do Mekhet practitioners of the Coil double dip? Do they both negate the -1 penalty from the Clan Bane and add their full dots in the Coil to their Humanity to the actual Bane calculation? If the Dragon learns the Coil before their Humanity drops to 6, does it prevent the Clan Bane from manifesting until their Humanity is 6 - (dots in the Coil)? It's unlikely, but I could see someone trying to spin it that way.<br /> <br /> I assume it has no impact on the &quot;great bane&quot; of sunlight, or else it's stepping on the Ascendants toes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think it's pretty clear that only stuff which directly references humanity get he bonus. So yeah, Ventrue don't benefit. Mekhet do, since their clan bane is to take up a bane which cares bout humanity. <br /> <br /> (Sorry for double post)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T13:23:43-07:00","id":293162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=293071#post293071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not an issue whatsoever, since anyone wanting to abuse it would also take Coil of Ascendant which gives immunity to fire frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>But is heavily stressed than following different Mysteries it's really an accomplishment by itself... I think it evens out, but even putting a limitation wouldn't be a problem..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2213-tittopaolo210","name":"TittoPaolo210","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T13:36:33-07:00","id":293165,"title":"","content":"Eh, any Vampire with Psychokinesis (Fire) is just <i>begging</i> for it. After all, running out of Willpower at an inappropriate time can mean that that candle they were about to be burned by is now a bonfire as hot as a blowtorch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T16:34:37-07:00","id":293293,"title":"","content":"In general, this preview feels like it is lacking a lot of the bite that the previous two had. The Crones and the Carthians had things that were a lot more impressive, frankly. And the Coils seem a little out of theme for what Mysteries are supposed to be. Unless they're expanding that in this book's fluff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T16:42:31-07:00","id":293296,"title":"","content":"Considering the point of the Mysteries is to basically help push the Ordo out of the vampiric condition and into the &quot;what the hell is that&quot; condition, the only one out of place is the second Mystery set, and even that fits into the idea of evolving out of the vampiric condition.<br /> <br /> Remember, the Ordo are the ...well, not the transhumanists of the bunch, but certainly the transvampiricists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T16:55:16-07:00","id":293301,"title":"","content":"And the end goal of their evolution is hotly debated within the Order. There is no unified stance on what a Dragon should eventually become.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T16:56:04-07:00","id":293302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gebbethine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=293293#post293293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Coils seem a little out of theme for what Mysteries are supposed to be. Unless they're expanding that in this book's fluff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering one is nearly extinct because it concerns itself with things outside of the normal focus of the Order's pursuits, and the other is apocryphal and its adherents often executed upon discovery because it runs directly counter to the Order's goals, I'm pretty sure being a little out of theme is their <i>raison d'etre</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T19:24:42-07:00","id":293355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=293301#post293301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the end goal of their evolution is hotly debated within the Order. There is no unified stance on what a Dragon should eventually become.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence the different Mysteries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T19:46:14-07:00","id":293360,"title":"","content":"My main concern is that I'd like more merits for other position leaders. We have Twilight Judge ... how about the Sworn of Mysteries and the Sworn of the Axe heads?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My horror roleplaying blog with a strong focus on World of Darkness and Call of Cthulhu can be found here: <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\">http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1248-laraqua","name":"Laraqua","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T20:06:12-07:00","id":293364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=293355#post293355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hence the different Mysteries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Precisely.<br /> <br /> Laraqua brings up a good point. Is Twilight Judge still meant to be a unique position within the Sworn of the Dying Light? If so it should be clarified that there can only be one in a given domain, and a station merit for each of the other Oathsworn would be fantastic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T21:20:52-07:00","id":293376,"title":"","content":"Okay, about the Coil of Zirnitra, you might want to specify how the vampires can learn supernatural merits. Can they just spend experience points? Do they need to jump through hoops like undergoing vision quests or being taught by a chi master or does someone have to perform a surgery to rewire their brains? <br /> <br /> In the first case, the vampire ought to have in character control over their development, in the other learning the merit is part of the story and the ST can make it as easy, difficult, or flat out impossible to learn a merit as they want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T22:09:27-07:00","id":293400,"title":"","content":"I have shown the Ordo Dracul merits to the other members of my group, and the response was pretty underwhelming. Whereas when I showed the the proposals for Crones and Carthians there were merits they were excited about, and there was some debate about what is OP and what isn't.<br /> <br /> Considering both players in my group are playing members of the Ordo Dracul and neither of us plan to use any of the offered merits, I think there may be a problem here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T01:34:43-07:00","id":293561,"title":"","content":"Oh a funny thing I thought of about Producer: Now since the fluff is that the merit doubles the potency of one's blood I imagine someone might ask the ST to let them double their blood pool, but any ST that would allow would have to know what they're doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T02:01:39-07:00","id":293563,"title":"","content":"The Coil of Zirnitra, first dot should specify that the Drawback occurs on every usage of the merit. As written at the moment, one could argue that it does not apply to Psychokinesis, and my gut feeling says it should <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T11:57:11-07:00","id":293985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=293302#post293302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering one is nearly extinct because it concerns itself with things outside of the normal focus of the Order's pursuits, and the other is apocryphal and its adherents often executed upon discovery because it runs directly counter to the Order's goals, I'm pretty sure being a little out of theme is their <i>raison d'etre</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Even so, I would have prefered more options that weren't exceptions to the rule, especially since Carthians and Crones didn't get that treatment.<br /> <br /> In general, I found the write-up a bit underwhelming, especially compared to the other two previews we've seen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T13:03:54-07:00","id":294061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gebbethine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=293985#post293985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even so, I would have prefered more options that weren't exceptions to the rule, especially since Carthians and Crones didn't get that treatment.<br /> <br /> In general, I found the write-up a bit underwhelming, especially compared to the other two previews we've seen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like deviant and heretical Mysteries are actually more in-theme with the Ordo Dracul than new Mysteries that fit within their usual paradigm. They're pretty thorough in their methodology, so any new Mystery would have to either be recently discovered, long since abandoned, outlawed, or a secret reserved for the most advanced members in order to really fit in without retconning the original presentation of only three Mysteries. YMMV, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T13:25:27-07:00","id":294084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=294061#post294061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like deviant and heretical Mysteries are actually more in-theme with the Ordo Dracul than new Mysteries that fit within their usual paradigm. They're pretty thorough in their methodology, so any new Mystery would have to either be recently discovered, long since abandoned, outlawed, or a secret reserved for the most advanced members in order to really fit in without retconning the original presentation of only three Mysteries. YMMV, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> At least what I got from the original presentation of three mysteries... is that those are just three mysteries, in no way the only ones and that adding new ones is pretty easy. And does not require any retconning what-so-ever. Those three are simply most common ones. There's plenty of space between &quot;one of the most common&quot; and &quot;abandoned, outlawed, or a secret reserved for the most advanced members&quot;. Anyways, I feel that the Coil of Zinitra will be much more common, then given in the book, simply by the nature of the fact, that it will be heavily sought out by the players <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (of course, this is just my gut feeling... I might be wrong here)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T13:41:56-07:00","id":294094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=293563#post293563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Coil of Zirnitra, first dot should specify that the Drawback occurs on every usage of the merit. As written at the moment, one could argue that it does not apply to Psychokinesis, and my gut feeling says it should <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Buh... that doesn't <i>even make any sense</i> with the Drawback in question.<br /> <br /> On topic, tho: gebbethine, the Ordo's rule is transcendence and spitting in the face of god/God/the gods/Xenu. I don't see how the new Mysteries are breaking that rule.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T13:44:04-07:00","id":294098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=294094#post294094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Buh... that doesn't <i>even make any sense</i> with the Drawback in question.<br /> <br /> On topic, tho: gebbethine, the Ordo's rule is transcendence and spitting in the face of god/God/the gods/Xenu. I don't see how the new Mysteries are breaking that rule.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How does it not make any sense? You use the Merit as you wish, and simultaneously the drawback fire's off? That's how it would work on other merits. You use them and no matter if it's a success or failure, the drawback fires off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T13:48:30-07:00","id":294102,"title":"","content":"The Mysteries in the core are only the most common ones. There are lots of other mysteries -- some heretical, some obsolete, some that never advanced past the second dot, some that are really amazing but that only a handful of Defiant have ever mastered. The Order has a strong theme of transcendence, but there's no one (or three) definitive paths to that transcendence, and different Mysteries reflect different Dragons' ideas about what transcendence even <i>is</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 10-28-2014, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T14:02:28-07:00","id":294137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=294098#post294098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> How does it not make any sense? You use the Merit as you wish, and simultaneously the drawback fire's off? That's how it would work on other merits. You use them and no matter if it's a success or failure, the drawback fires off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh, I see the issue.<br /> <br /> I'm reading that clause as &quot;any Drawbacks that trigger on a Failure always trigger, success or failure&quot;, and you're reading it as &quot;every time you use it, the Drawback triggers.&quot;<br /> <br /> Gotcha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T14:19:20-07:00","id":294148,"title":"","content":"One thing I'd love to see would be more scales for the &quot;basic three&quot;, new stuff to make them more interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T14:38:26-07:00","id":294157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=294137#post294137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ahh, I see the issue.<br /> <br /> I'm reading that clause as &quot;any Drawbacks that trigger on a Failure always trigger, success or failure&quot;, and you're reading it as &quot;every time you use it, the Drawback triggers.&quot;<br /> <br /> Gotcha.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to be honest, that's how I WANT to read it. Since it's really strange, it really feels like the drawback should trigger there, as otherwise, some powers trigger these and some don't? It really feels like a shortcoming of the coil, as there it lists the power as harder to use, but, one of the most commonly taken powers (pyrokinesis) will go around this. <br /> <br /> That's why I'm asking for it to be changed into &quot;all use ages of the merit trigger the drawback&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T14:47:50-07:00","id":294166,"title":"","content":"To be fair, I read it as &quot;Using it triggers the drawback everytime&quot; as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T14:59:08-07:00","id":294178,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I'd go for City-Walking first. I love that Merit <i>so much</i>.<br /> <br /> If my ST were to rule Clear Sighted as a Supernatural Merit, I'd pick it up first as well; seeing through Obfuscate and Nightmare is <i>damn useful</i>, and seems like something that an Ordo member would cultivate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T16:17:10-07:00","id":294259,"title":"","content":"I'm sure wordcount is spare enough as it is, but I feel like Grafting Unholy Flesh would benefit greatly from a sidebar with guidelines on what should or shouldn't count as an &quot;ability&quot; that they can graft. It doesn't have to be exhaustive (and realistically it can't even be close) but a good litmus test should be able to help STs out with adjucating an otherwise extremely broad and vague power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T18:04:05-07:00","id":294358,"title":"","content":"Anyone having flashbacks of Eclipse Caste Solars when they read &quot;The Coil of Zirnitra&quot; and, more importantly, Grafting Unholy Flesh? I like the -idea- of it, but this is one of those things that is going to go into a very bad place very quickly.<br /> <br /> Also, are you really making half vampires and werewolf vampires default, if rare, canon? ... And Telepathic Vampires. Not gonna lie, smidge of a e_e kneejerk reaction there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T19:04:23-07:00","id":294410,"title":"","content":"Vampires are already telepathic. Auspex says hi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T19:23:11-07:00","id":294420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=294358#post294358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone having flashbacks of Eclipse Caste Solars when they read &quot;The Coil of Zirnitra&quot; and, more importantly, Grafting Unholy Flesh? I like the -idea- of it, but this is one of those things that is going to go into a very bad place very quickly.<br /> <br /> Also, are you really making half vampires and werewolf vampires default, if rare, canon? ... And Telepathic Vampires. Not gonna lie, smidge of a e_e kneejerk reaction there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> and Dead Wolves bloodline from Shadows of Mexico book says hi as well. They're the one's who can contribute dots to Totem Merit for a werewolf pack, and thus they can join werewolf packs as proper members and are pretty much half vampires and have werewolves already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T19:26:56-07:00","id":294424,"title":"","content":"I kind of want a Dead Wolves for VtR 2nd Ed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T19:30:43-07:00","id":294429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=294358#post294358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone having flashbacks of Eclipse Caste Solars when they read &quot;The Coil of Zirnitra&quot; and, more importantly, Grafting Unholy Flesh? I like the -idea- of it, but this is one of those things that is going to go into a very bad place very quickly.<br /> <br /> Also, are you really making half vampires and werewolf vampires default, if rare, canon? ... And Telepathic Vampires. Not gonna lie, smidge of a e_e kneejerk reaction there.</div> </div> </div> </div>We have Solars in WoD now?<br /> <br /> Also, vampires have always been telepathic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T19:44:03-07:00","id":294430,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I don't see the new Coil as problematic as people seem to be making it out to be from a balance perspective. Unlike oWoD, this is specifically limited to mortal only powers which means we are not dealing with Vampires who can cast Time/Fate 5 arcana to boot. Some powers are certainly powerful when paired with natural Kindred powers and abilities, but if you throw all of your experience into gaining dots in the coil, you are at a minimum looking at 105 experience and that is assuming you buy nothing else at all. Sure you may have 5 dots in coils, but then the Kindred Moroi will simply chop you into bits while the Dominate 5 Kindred orders you around like a small puppy.<br /> <br /> Hell, the coil doesn't even grant you the merit for free, that is yet more experience you need to toss into making it effective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T21:47:23-07:00","id":294518,"title":"","content":"Any mechanic that rapidly expands the scope of what someone can do in relation to &quot;normal&quot; options with little to no cost will almost always end poorly, unless the game is designed to handle that. You can say that Vampire Disciplines are by and large more powerful than anything they can buy through this coil, but that's exactly the reasoning that created the Eclipse problem. You'll run into hedge cases where the merits are better and/or cheaper than the discipline alternatives. Yes an ST can exorcise &quot;common sense,&quot; but that assumes the ST is more familiar with the game mechanics than their player and has that kind of foresight. Not every ST will catch every hedge case, nor should they be expected to.<br /> <br /> Narratively there's a bit of dissonance as well. The mechanics encourage the vampire to expand different psychic abilities rather than focus on &quot;reclaiming&quot; one or two and how that impacts their Requiem. This works for a hedge mage, but less so for a psychic. Admittedly, this can be fixed with a slight adjustment to the fluff.<br /> <br /> That said, the coil isn't really <i>that</i> bad. Vampire is a game framed in a way where this sort of thing can be kept under control. In contrast, Grafting the Unholy Flesh is just a really, really bad idea. It allows a rapid expansion of power with little to no oversight or cost. Yes, there is the fluff cost of having to actually go about the grafting process but even taking that into consideration, it still drastically the rate of power growth. Its also somewhat vague on what counts as &quot;one power.&quot; If you take a Vampire's Eyes to get their Auspex, and they have Auspex 5... do you get all 5 dots (with &quot;Auspex&quot; being the power) or do you get only a single level?<br /> <br /> What's a shame is I do actually like the fluff and the potential stories opened up by Grafting the Unholy Flesh being used responsibly. I just know it won't be used responsibly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 10-28-2014, 12:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T01:03:25-07:00","id":294611,"title":"","content":"For completion's sake and because I finally can have a nice avatar on these forums, I repost my entry from the comments section here:<br /> <br /> I see almost no point in Shedding the Beast\u2019s Skin (The Coil of Ziva 5).<br /> <br /> This is almost the same as the Blush of Life (B&amp;S p.90):\u201dBy spending a point of Vitae, Kindred may invoke the blush of life for a scene. This makes them functionally human. They become warm to the touch, with a full, hearty pulse. They produce natural bodily fluids. They function sexually in the way a human can, becoming physically aroused, erect, and lubricated. They can keep food and drink down, ejecting it later in the night. They\u2019ll pass medical inspection while the blush remains active.\u201d<br /> The Warm Face (Coil of the Ascendant 2; B&amp;S p. 156) can even make the Blush of Life last 24 hours.<br /> What would make Shedding the Beast\u2019s Skin interesting IMHO would be immunity to ALL vampire banes, not just the <i>clan </i>banes, i.e. no more damage from sunlight, no need for daysleep etc, not subject to frenzy.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1281-aegontargaryen","name":"AegonTargaryen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1281_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T01:31:25-07:00","id":294615,"title":"","content":"The developers are watching both the forums and the comment section there, so there's no need to double post stuff in both places <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T02:17:14-07:00","id":294637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=294430#post294430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I don't see the new Coil as problematic as people seem to be making it out to be from a balance perspective. Unlike oWoD, this is specifically limited to mortal only powers which means we are not dealing with Vampires who can cast Time/Fate 5 arcana to boot. Some powers are certainly powerful when paired with natural Kindred powers and abilities, but if you throw all of your experience into gaining dots in the coil, you are at a minimum looking at 105 experience and that is assuming you buy nothing else at all. Sure you may have 5 dots in coils, but then the Kindred Moroi will simply chop you into bits while the Dominate 5 Kindred orders you around like a small puppy.<br /> <br /> Hell, the coil doesn't even grant you the merit for free, that is yet more experience you need to toss into making it effective.</div> </div> </div> </div>...where are you getting 21 XP? This is a Vampire 2e Coil, where the costing is <i>completely different</i>.<br /> <br /> If you take the Mystery of Zirnitra as your &quot;focus&quot; Mystery, each dot costs 3xp, for a total of 15xp. Even if it isn't, it just costs 20xp.<br /> <br /> And you can start off with 3 dots if you <i>really</i> feel like it. EDIT: I just reread the book, and I'm wrong on this one. You can have 1 dot at character creation, not 3.<br /> <br /> Heck, one of the new merits (which got some discussion earlier on) would reduce that to 2xp per dot.<br /> <br /> And SoulGambit... the power of the Coil <i>is</i> enormously dependent on ST fiat - the Coil lets you buy mortal-only <i>Supernatural</i> merits, a set whose only explicit members are in the GMC appendix and the new Merits doc. It's up to the ST to decide whether things like Clear Sighted or Producer count as Supernatural merits in their game. So it's less of a &quot;can STs catch every edge case&quot; and more &quot;what Merits will they let it apply to?&quot;<br /> <br /> I do agree that <i>maybe</i> it could be more focused... but I see focusing on <b>one</b> Merit for a whole Coil as kinda ridiculous. Maybe they could have a Scale that boosted their Coil rating for the purposes of a single Merit, so that a former Electrokinetic could buy one dot in the Coil and then use &lt;Insert Cool Scale Name Here&gt; to act like they have an extra 2-3 dots. That could be something to look into...<br /> <br /> ...Especially <i>instead</i> of Grafting Unholy Flesh. I mean, I'm all for grafting stuff on bodies, don't get me wrong - but this is a Scale that lets you steal a Demon's ability to lie perfectly (take their tongue), another Vampire's Disciplines/Devotions, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 10-28-2014, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T05:37:39-07:00","id":294726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AegonTargaryen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=294611#post294611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> For completion's sake and because I finally can have a nice avatar on these forums, I repost my entry from the comments section here:<br /> <br /> I see almost no point in Shedding the Beast\u2019s Skin (The Coil of Ziva 5).<br /> <br /> This is almost the same as the Blush of Life (B&amp;S p.90):\u201dBy spending a point of Vitae, Kindred may invoke the blush of life for a scene. This makes them functionally human. They become warm to the touch, with a full, hearty pulse. They produce natural bodily fluids. They function sexually in the way a human can, becoming physically aroused, erect, and lubricated. They can keep food and drink down, ejecting it later in the night. They\u2019ll pass medical inspection while the blush remains active.\u201d<br /> The Warm Face (Coil of the Ascendant 2; B&amp;S p. 156) can even make the Blush of Life last 24 hours.<br /> What would make Shedding the Beast\u2019s Skin interesting IMHO would be immunity to ALL vampire banes, not just the <i>clan </i>banes, i.e. no more damage from sunlight, no need for daysleep etc, not subject to frenzy.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I am fairly certain it is not really meant as a mechanical upgrade. In fact, to me it seems implied you also become vulnerable like a mortal again. It is a roleplaying thing, not done to get a mechanical advantage (although it might be one in some circumstances). If it was indeed purely beneficial it would probably be not (as) heretical to the Ordo Dracul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T05:43:32-07:00","id":294730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=294726#post294726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am fairly certain it is not really meant as a mechanical upgrade.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shedding the Beast's Skin is a 5 dot Discipline power. It should probably have some kind of mechanical effect befitting its level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T05:57:05-07:00","id":294735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=294730#post294730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shedding the Beast's Skin is a 5 dot Discipline power. It should probably have some kind of mechanical effect befitting its level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Should it, really? This would be a similar argument like the one about why or why not a Promethean would want to become human. It is a power meant for players or storytellers who want to portray specific stories, not really as a random upgrade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T06:42:07-07:00","id":294781,"title":"","content":"Absolutely it should. I'm not even close to saying that vampires becoming human again (even temporarily) is a bad thing. I <i>like</i> Shedding, but I think it's underwhelming for a 5 dot power. It could be an awesome Scale, but the ability to become human and walk in the sun unharmed is pretty boss given the lax restrictions on what Scales any Dragon can learn.<br /> <br /> The story crafting and thematic potential of Shedding is great, but the mechanical benefits are not quite there. To justify the investment in both in-game stories and Experiences to rise to mastery in a Coil it should deliver on both fronts.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T06:50:51-07:00","id":294784,"title":"","content":"Let's not forget, that in B&amp;S, most 5th dots are not as strong as they used to be. Now the biggest part of the punch is in the first three dots of the disciplines, last two being there for some added utility, and for some more scaling of effects of the earlier powers. This one accomplishes that perfectly, and has a ton of mechanical punch behind it (you're functionally human... it's uber strong, in my opinion, there's so much one can do. No fear of the beast (Wanna meet loved ones?) Infiltrating the hunter nests, doing other awesome stuff .It's much more potent than Protean 5, in my opinion, which simply turns you into a hungry mist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T07:06:09-07:00","id":294788,"title":"","content":"I'm certainly not comparing it to 1e Disciplines.<br /> <br /> That said, having thought through it more the ability to walk in the sun regardless of Humanity and Blood Potency is super powerful, and extremely cool. As I said above, <i>way</i> too powerful for a Scale, so that ability does belong right where it is. The rest of it feels like fluff that kind of buries the lead. Yes, it's cool to be a physically functional human being and the ability to create actual children is boundless story fodder. But as far as power utility goes the shedding of all Banes, including sunlight, is crazy good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T08:57:05-07:00","id":294896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=294615#post294615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The developers are watching both the forums and the comment section there, so there's no need to double post stuff in both places <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. I'm reading and taking notes, both on the blog and the forum.<br /> <br /> EDIT: By the way, on Producer specifically... I'm coming around to the thinking that infinite fuel effects just shouldn't be allowed, rather than writing around them every time. They're usually just quirks of the way we abstract things like energy and damage, rather than in-setting implications of powers, so there shouldn't be any harm in just nullifying the effect like most STs would anyway. Would have been good to decide that when we were doing the core, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 10-28-2014, 12:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T16:21:11-07:00","id":295361,"title":"","content":"Did nobody notice that Siphon The Soul doesn't kill the victim unless Diablerie is committed also? Its just a partial diablerie that has a somewhat opposite effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T16:53:47-07:00","id":295382,"title":"","content":"I don't think that went unnoticed, no.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Though that brings up a good point. If a Dragon steals a point of Humanity using Siphon Soul, then continues to full-blown Amaranth, is that 2 detachment checks, or just 1?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","user":"Smarmy Vamp","date":". 10-28-2014, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T01:12:55-07:00","id":295666,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">When </span>the effect of Shedding the Beast\u2019s Skin ends, the user<span style=\"color:#000000\"> becomes Kindred again: &quot;<i>For nearly a half an hour, she undergoes the sensations and transformations of the Embrace again. This leaves her functionally incapacitated during this time.</i></span></span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Wouldn't it be appropriate for this traumatic experience also to cause a Humanity roll ? It would also be quite ironic that those who struggle to become Human again run into danger of losing their humanity when they <i>almost</i> succeed. This also would set a limit to using the power if it does include walking in the sun without harm. Imagine a Vampire becoming addicted to walking in daylight again, but slowly loosing his humanity in the process ...</span> Maybe she then turns to Syphon the Soul tom prevent this, but that will get her into lot of different trouble ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1281-aegontargaryen","user":"AegonTargaryen","date":". 10-29-2014, 04:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1281-aegontargaryen","name":"AegonTargaryen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1281_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T01:46:17-07:00","id":295674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AegonTargaryen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=295666#post295666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">When </span>the effect of Shedding the Beast\u2019s Skin ends, the user<span style=\"color:#000000\"> becomes Kindred again: &quot;<i>For nearly a half an hour, she undergoes the sensations and transformations of the Embrace again. This leaves her functionally incapacitated during this time.</i></span></span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Wouldn't it be appropriate for this traumatic experience also to cause a Humanity roll ? It would also be quite ironic that those who struggle to become Human again run into danger of losing their humanity when they <i>almost</i> succeed. This also would set a limit to using the power if it does include walking in the sun without harm. Imagine a Vampire becoming addicted to walking in daylight again, but slowly loosing his humanity in the process ...</span> Maybe she then turns to Syphon the Soul tom prevent this, but that will get her into lot of different trouble ...</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see it being a Breaking Point at humanity 6 or 5. Not much lower tho...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T00:17:17-07:00","id":296716,"title":"","content":"Which banes does Denying the Bane apply to? Humanity affects sunlight, torpor, clan, and bane banes.<br /> <br /> How does Denying the Bane work with Clan Banes?<br /> <br /> Daeva roll Humanity<br /> Gangrel have a roll cap of Humanity<br /> Mekhet affect on chosen bane is obvious, but there is sunlight and torpor<br /> Nosferatu have a Humanity penalty on some rolls<br /> Ventrue appear to be unaffected<br /> <br /> If &quot;add dots of the Coil to Humanity&quot; is the answer when it comes to Clan Banes then I'm reading it correctly. There is still some ambiguity regarding sunlight and torpor. The text would appear to include them as well.<br /> <br /> As an aside, I have no problem with vampires playing with fire. My surprise was after the &quot;Law can do things sorcery can't&quot; rumblings, I expected some since a Coil allows a merit that controls and creates fire, another thing beyond sorcery. I guess those rumblings were coming from the Law taking on mystical attributes. Dragons and fire. Makes sense to me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 10-30-2014, 03:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T00:51:57-07:00","id":296744,"title":"","content":"All of the banes which scale with Humanity.<br /> So Daeva roll more.<br /> Gangrel's cap is higher.<br /> Mekhet's scaling is pretty obvious.<br /> Nosferatu are unaffected.<br /> Ventrue are unaffected.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't see any ambiguity, it talks about banes which scale from humanity, so sunlight and torpor is counted in.<br /> <br /> EDIT: If you want more reasoning on Nosferatu, here it is: Nosferatu clan bane does NOT scale with humanity. Their bane is: Your Humanity is counted as TWO lower, for the purpose of Humanity penalties. So their bane do not scale in any way according to humanity <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> They just get it harsher with usual vampire penalties, which are not a bane.<br /> <br /> EDIT2: Of course, this creates a strange place, where the Coil is much better for other clans. Perhaps a small house rule/addition? If you have 2 dots of coil, Nosferatu count their penalty as 1, if you have 5 dots, it counts as +0? For mekhet, I'm not even sure <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (well at least for me, it's not an issue, since I use a houseruled version of Ventrue bane, which does scale with Humanity)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":294,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","user":"Griautis","date":". 10-30-2014, 03:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T01:51:16-07:00","id":296768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=294730#post294730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shedding the Beast's Skin is a 5 dot Discipline power. It should probably have some kind of mechanical effect befitting its level.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if you'd consider it commensurate, but the intention was to make the change sufficient that: <br /> <br /> 1) Nobody could prove you were Kindred. No Predatory Aura at all.<br /> <br /> 2) While a secondary effect, it would get rid of any bashing damage your character suffered. For Kindred, that can be a lot. <br /> <br /> 3) Being able to birth children is a huge story effect. Maybe not directly mechanical, but huge for plot. <br /> <br /> 4) You could use it to dump a vampire hunter's trail. &quot;What are you talking about? I'm human. I bleed. I eat. I fuck. I sweat. See? No fangs. Also, the sun has no effect on me. Now, why don't you go on home and take some Xanax?&quot; <br /> <br /> 5) Again, not mechanical directly, but this gives an ideal opportunity to explore and study The Embrace without any Humanity concerns. And doing so first person. <br /> <br /> 6) Blood Sympathy is one of the best ways a revenant can find you if you accidentally created one. The Sheriff uses your revenant as a blood hound to find you? You can nope right out of it. <br /> <br /> That said, I don't know what notes Rose might have, but I think I might offer a couple more clear-cut advantages in the final draft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T01:55:30-07:00","id":296769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=296768#post296768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure if you'd consider it commensurate, but the intention was to make the change sufficient that:<br /> <br /> 1) Nobody could prove you were Kindred. No Predatory Aura at all.<br /> <br /> 2) While a secondary effect, it would get rid of any bashing damage your character suffered. For Kindred, that can be a lot.<br /> <br /> 3) Being able to birth children is a huge story effect. Maybe not directly mechanical, but huge for plot.<br /> <br /> 4) You could use it to dump a vampire hunter's trail. &quot;What are you talking about? I'm human. I bleed. I eat. I fuck. I sweat. See? No fangs. Also, the sun has no effect on me. Now, why don't you go on home and take some Xanax?&quot;<br /> <br /> 5) Again, not mechanical directly, but this gives an ideal opportunity to explore and study The Embrace without any Humanity concerns. And doing so first person.<br /> <br /> 6) Blood Sympathy is one of the best ways a revenant can find you if you accidentally created one. The Sheriff uses your revenant as a blood hound to find you? You can nope right out of it.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't know what notes Rose might have, but I think I might offer a couple more clear-cut advantages in the final draft.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Those are pretty obvious and as Swarmy Vamp later said, the power is fine as it is. There's no reason to enumerate the ways it can be useful <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Just perhaps underlining, that for ALL intents and purposes, you're a human, until the time is up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T03:48:53-07:00","id":296874,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm on board with Shedding the Beast's Skin, it just took a few spins through the noggin to get there. When I started thinking about whether or not it would make a better Scale than a Coil power, it became clear that its benefits are really huge. Not sure why it snuck in through the side door, but my theory is that the description opens with more subtle aspects of the power. Hiding from hunters because your heart beats is hardly worthy of a 5 dot Coil, every vampire can already do that with Blush of Health. Perhaps if the final draft starts with the big bombs like like sunlight, makin' babies, no frenzy, then it wouldn't have that problem<br /> <br /> Regarding the discussion of Denying the Bane, is torpor considered a Bane to which it would apply? I never thought of it as a specific Bane, more like what happens to a vampire instead of, ya know, dying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T04:30:39-07:00","id":296938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=296874#post296874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'm on board with Shedding the Beast's Skin, it just took a few spins through the noggin to get there. When I started thinking about whether or not it would make a better Scale than a Coil power, it became clear that its benefits are really huge. Not sure why it snuck in through the side door, but my theory is that the description opens with more subtle aspects of the power. Hiding from hunters because your heart beats is hardly worthy of a 5 dot Coil, every vampire can already do that with Blush of Health. Perhaps if the final draft starts with the big bombs like like sunlight, makin' babies, no frenzy, then it wouldn't have that problem<br /> <br /> Regarding the discussion of Denying the Bane, is torpor considered a Bane to which it would apply? I never thought of it as a specific Bane, more like what happens to a vampire instead of, ya know, dying.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a really good question. I've never really considered torpor a bane, per se. Like you said, it's kind of an alternative to dying. Kind of like how I don't consider staking a bane; it's actually a preferable situation to a human's heart being pierced. But I totally see how it could be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T07:12:24-07:00","id":297087,"title":"","content":"Staking a vampire is like witch ducking, either way you're screwed. If you drown/bleed to death you were human but you're still dead. Whoops better luck next time. If you float/don't bleed; it's a monster, burn it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T16:59:54-07:00","id":297602,"title":"","content":"Under the Mekhet clan bane, torpor is listed as a bane to which the humanity penalty applies. I guess the bane aspect is the length of torpor.<br /> <br /> @Grat There is no mention of banes that scale in the Coil. It simply says add Coil to Humanity when determining bane effects. Ex: The effect of the Nosferatu bane is subtracting 2 from Humanity for a Social penalty. This could easily be considered Coil + Humanity - 2 for Social.<br /> <br /> I think torpor as a bane is ambiguous to many people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 10-30-2014, 08:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T17:22:04-07:00","id":297632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=297602#post297602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think torpor as a bane is ambiguous to many people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems that way. I'm one of those people that doesn't consider it a bane, though the wording of the Mekhet clan bane makes it murky. Given that wording I'm inclined to let the Coil add to the Mekhet's Humanity (and seems odd that it would work for them, but not anyone else). Clarification would rock some number of socks.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu seems a no-brainer to benefit from the added Coil dots.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T00:52:15-07:00","id":297920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=297602#post297602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Grat There is no mention of banes that scale in the Coil. It simply says add Coil to Humanity when determining bane effects. Ex: The effect of the Nosferatu bane is subtracting 2 from Humanity for a Social penalty. This could easily be considered Coil + Humanity - 2 for Social.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's clearly not how it's supposed to work. A coil about reducing effects of Banes, giving a bonus to it? What? And you said exactly the truth Determining Bane effects. Bane effect is -2 to humanity, it has noway to scale here. You can't apply the effect to a subsequent system, which in itself is not considered a bane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T07:50:46-07:00","id":298130,"title":"","content":"&quot;Add her Coil dots to her Humanity for the purpose of determining the effects of her Banes. This includes her clan Bane.&quot;<br /> <br /> It seems like it's intended to work, to me.<br /> <br /> The Mysteries are specifically called out as a way to circumvent banes in <i>Blood and Smoke</i>. Now... how does it interact with the Ventrue bane, if at all? My first thought is it doesn't.<br /> <br /> I could also see it offsetting penalties in the Mekhet and Nosferatu banes, but not actually providing any kind of effective bonus beyond the vampire's actual Humanity. So a Humanity 5 Nosferatu with Coil of Ziva 5 still only counts as Humanity 5 for social penalties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","user":"Smarmy Vamp","date":". 10-31-2014, 10:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T09:18:29-07:00","id":298219,"title":"","content":"Yeah, there's already a mechanical precedent for mitigating penalties without adding bonuses. Though in a case like the Daeva clan bane, I imagine it just adds to the dicepool to resist becoming obsessed with the victim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T12:37:19-07:00","id":298366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=298130#post298130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Mysteries are specifically called out as a way to circumvent banes in <i>Blood and Smoke</i>. Now... how does it interact with the Ventrue bane, if at all? My first thought is it doesn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it doesn't have an obvious application for the Ventrue bane, unless it just negates it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T14:35:17-07:00","id":298412,"title":"","content":"So Rites of the Impaled was a hit with my Tzimisce player (I run VtM using the NWoD system) and he'll probably end up taking it when he gets the Experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T17:34:31-07:00","id":298563,"title":"","content":"My bad. The formula I meant would be (Coils - 2, MAX = 0) + Humanity for Nossies. I see no way for it to interact with the Ventrue bane. You can't go back. Although, I could see someone saying otherwise. That Coil gets weird with Clan Banes. I'm not the writer or developer so I can't say what the intention is of either. That is why I asked all the questions about it. When I know how it is supposed to work then we can talk about if the wording reflects that.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 10-31-2014, 08:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T18:48:28-07:00","id":298603,"title":"","content":"This is my understanding of Denying the Bane.<br /> <br /> Bane banes are straightforward, mostly. The only question would be if Humanity + Coil of Ziva caps at 10.<br /> <br /> Sunlight damage and duration of torpor are equally straightforward, if they are affected, with the same question as above.<br /> <br /> Clan Banes<br /> Daeva add Coil of Ziva to Humanity for the roll on the second or further drinks.<br /> Gangrel add Coil of Ziva to Humanity to determine the pool cap.<br /> Mekhet lose their penalty on &quot;Humanity-based banes (including sunlight and torpor)&quot; and their chosen bane is treated as above. Still have one less bane choice.<br /> Nosferatu treat their Humanity as only one less, or with further Coil mastery none less, but still treats failures as dramatic failures.<br /> Ventrue are unaffected.<br /> <br /> So Daeva, Gangrel, Mekhet and Nosferatu still have some bane left which makes sense, more incentive to continue the path. The Gangrel have a niche case where their bane is effectively gone with high Humanity and/or Coil mastery. I doubt it matters. Ventrue are unaffected. There is a way to change that, but I'm not going to bother.<br /> <br /> I would assume that Humanity + Coil of Ziva caps at 10. I would prefer sunlight and torpor including with clan bane, if they are affected by this Coil. I don't object to their inclusion. I do think that would make this Coil abnormally broadly reaching in it's effects for the first dot of a Coil. Practically, I don't think it is abnormally powerful, just broad. If I'm wrong on how the way it works with clan banes then I might need some clarifications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T21:19:30-07:00","id":298662,"title":"","content":"That's how I've been looking at it as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T04:10:47-07:00","id":298824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=298603#post298603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is my understanding of Denying the Bane.<br /> <br /> Bane banes are straightforward, mostly. The only question would be if Humanity + Coil of Ziva caps at 10.<br /> <br /> Sunlight damage and duration of torpor are equally straightforward, if they are affected, with the same question as above.<br /> <br /> Clan Banes<br /> Daeva add Coil of Ziva to Humanity for the roll on the second or further drinks.<br /> Gangrel add Coil of Ziva to Humanity to determine the pool cap.<br /> Mekhet lose their penalty on &quot;Humanity-based banes (including sunlight and torpor)&quot; and their chosen bane is treated as above. Still have one less bane choice.<br /> Nosferatu treat their Humanity as only one less, or with further Coil mastery none less, but still treats failures as dramatic failures.<br /> Ventrue are unaffected.<br /> <br /> So Daeva, Gangrel, Mekhet and Nosferatu still have some bane left which makes sense, more incentive to continue the path. The Gangrel have a niche case where their bane is effectively gone with high Humanity and/or Coil mastery. I doubt it matters. Ventrue are unaffected. There is a way to change that, but I'm not going to bother.<br /> <br /> I would assume that Humanity + Coil of Ziva caps at 10. I would prefer sunlight and torpor including with clan bane, if they are affected by this Coil. I don't object to their inclusion. I do think that would make this Coil abnormally broadly reaching in it's effects for the first dot of a Coil. Practically, I don't think it is abnormally powerful, just broad. If I'm wrong on how the way it works with clan banes then I might need some clarifications.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And I disagree with the Mekhet entirely. You just get your bonus on the bane itself, which you gained there. You don't get to double down on that by both reducing the Mekhet penalty, and then subsequently adding to the bane.<br /> Same with Nosferatu, that's not supported by the text, as treating your humanity higher, does not in any way, decrease the -2 penalty, because it's not dependant on your humanity. So unless specific cases of how the coil works with those three clans happen - they're unaffected.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Quoting the text: &quot; <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Add her Coil dots to her Humanity for the purpose of determining the effects of her Banes. This includes her clan Bane.&quot;</span></span></span> So yeah, your humanity is increased for banes,. However, if the same bane does not reference humanity, there's no scaling. That's exactly where Mekhet and Nosferatu fall in. They're banes have static numbers (-2) in there, which do not scale with humanity, that's why the bane does not affect them. <br /> <br /> Any scaling added there, is either a house rule, or a completely false reading of the rules, as they are written. Tho, I do hope, that some effects for Mekhet,Nosferatu,Ventrue might be appended <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":294,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","user":"Griautis","date":". 11-01-2014, 07:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T06:59:25-07:00","id":298918,"title":"","content":"I see what you're saying, Griautis. I just think that if the intent of the Coil power is to mitigate banes, Nosferatu and Mekhet (and if you want to get a little overly complex, Ventrue) have Humanity-related bane effects that Denying the Bane should help with.<br /> <br /> Clarifying the intent and effects is necessary, here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T08:17:04-07:00","id":298936,"title":"","content":"Oh, of course. If the intent is such, we need to write up additional effects for them. However, as written, it cannot be stretched to cover that ground (unless, as I mentioned, house rules). <br /> <br /> And I do agree that the coil should be more or less good enough for all the clans - and it is not such as written. Anyways, hopefully that will be clarified.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T15:03:28-07:00","id":299341,"title":"","content":"I'm not trying to argue about it. The Nosferatu and Mekhet have effectively a penalty on their Humanity score in certain situations. The Coil is meant to mitigate the effect on banes of lower Humanity so it makes sense to me for the Coil to overcome those penalties. If we read it two different ways then I think that is a great example of clarification needed. I can live with the Ventrue not be affected, but the Nosferatu need some love from the Coil. If only 3 out of 5 of the Clans get a benefit then it really isn't true to say it affects Clan Banes. It would affect some, maybe it should be none. One Clan is fine since we are talking about a Bane that many people have house rules for anyway. I think everyone keeps the Nosferatu as written, so they need to be affected in some way. They would be the type to want to get this Coil to get a better connection to Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T16:59:22-07:00","id":299464,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm going by the DIRECT wording of the coil. If we need to make up our own effects, to stretch it far enough toi cover other banes - it's wrong wording, or it is not meant to cover those places. So in my opinion, either the wording needs to be changed, or nossies and ventrues get no benefit from it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T18:10:22-07:00","id":299518,"title":"","content":"Nor do Daeva.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T20:37:18-07:00","id":299610,"title":"","content":"Daeva roll Humanity to resist their Clan Bane. They, and Gangrel, are the ones that most clearly benefit from &quot;Add her Coil dots to her Humanity for the purpose of determining the effects of her Banes. This includes her Clan Banes.&quot; Mekhet and Nosferatu are questionable, but there are ways to interpret the Coil that benefit them. In particular, I'd like a clarification on how the Coil works for Mekhet. Do they double dip by negating the penalty from the clan bane and adding the full Coil dots to the Bane calculation itself? Ventrue pretty much get no benefit unless you go with a very broad interpretation of the Coil's power, but then again, the Ventrue Clan Bane isn't really that serious from a mechanical standpoint anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T09:01:16-08:00","id":300035,"title":"","content":"As I said before, only stuff which directly scales from humanity get the benefit. There's no &quot;interpretation&quot; to be done, only house rules, so please stop confusing things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T20:16:53-08:00","id":300682,"title":"","content":"I 100% agree that Twilight Judge needs to be reworked and toned down a lot! There should actually be a mechanic attached to it instead of something automatically happening that way there is some defense against it. The way it reads it sounds like everyone has to be your bitch if they are Ordo. A preq must be that they are Sworn of Dying Light.<br /> <br /> The Coil of Ziva seems to be all over the place. It kind of feels like the old Locus and Anushka's ladder mixed in, which are completely opposite concepts. The whole Pseudo Diablarie does not make sense and seems way too evil to the point of automatic degeneration.<br /> <br /> Shedding the Beast Skin feels more like a 5 dot Scale for Coil of the Ascendant with it's theme. You can still say it is heretical as I can still see that.<br /> <br /> Denying the Bane (1 dot Coil) feels like a way more powerful version of Epidermal Shielding Bath (5 Dot Scale).<br /> <br /> Buttress the Soul should simply give a bonus to the roll equal to dot rating in in the coil. This would better reflect a characters mastery over the coil. Spending blood feels cheap and anyone can do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1852-maskah","name":"Maskah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T05:09:36-08:00","id":300991,"title":"","content":"I don't think Twilight Judge needs to be &quot;toned down a lot&quot; per se, I just think it needs to be noted whether there's supposed to be one per domain as is laid out in the Ordo Dracul book, or if you can have a cadre of Twilight Judges. The merit has a ton of potential, but it gets weird if you have multiple people running around using it. It doesn't automatically make every other Dragon your bitch, you really don't have any direct sway over what they do. You can leverage them if they study, or want to study, a heretical Coil, and you have access to any Coil you want to study. It's certainly very cool, but I wouldn't say it's a problem at all. It definitely should have Sworn as a prerequisite.<br /> <br /> EDIT: If in fact there can be more than one Twilight Judge, maybe a note that the higher Covenant Status Judge trumps others.<br /> <br /> I originally thought the Coil of Ziva was oddly formulated as well, but I've come around after a little rumination. It's totally a combination of Anoushka's Ladder and Way of the Locust, and I think that's okay. Instead of a &quot;little goody two shoes&quot; Golconda-lite power, you retain your Humanity through force and ultimately theft. It's a brutal contradiction, and right up the Ordo Dracul's re-defined alley. You're going to keep your Beast at bay on your own terms by any means necessary, and anyone who gives you shit about it just might be next against the wall when it's time to boost the Man another notch over the Beast. Spending Vitae to guard against degeneration is fun too. Totally Coiling the curse back against itself.<br /> <br /> The problem with Scales is that you don't actually need the high prerequisite dots to develop them. A lowly 1-dot Coil Dragon who follows any Mystery at all could develop Shedding the Beast's Skin if it was a Scale. Just costs 1 more experience, that you can offset with a Crucible! That's not really okay.<br /> <br /> Again, the 5 dot Scale thing for Epidermal Shielding Bath only matters to the tune of 1 experience. Additionally, Epidermal Shielding Bath can be used to protect <i>other</i> vampires, not just the Dragon who knows the Scale. You can make your whole coterie highly resistant to sunlight. The potential there should not be understated. Denying the Bane is broad in scope, and very cool, but it's personal.<br /> <br /> One of the basic building blocks of Coils is that they give you new ways to utilize Vitae, so spending Vitae for bonuses to resist Degeneration seems good. It also ties in to the concept of coiling the curse back on itself, as I mentioned above. It also makes Blood Potency the limiting factor on how much of a bonus you get from the Coil, rather than the Coil dots itself. That last one is a matter of preference and design choice, but I like it. More powerful Blood means you can leverage it against the curse more effectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T05:16:01-08:00","id":300994,"title":"","content":"Thoughts on Perilous Nest: This is an extremely powerful intrusion deterrent. When it says the attacks of the Nest can cause bashing damage, or cost a Willpower point, is that meant to represent different kinds of attacks? For damage you have poltergeists throwing stuff at intruders, or the objects in the place animate, slam doors on them, etc. Then for Willpower attacks you have horrifying hauntings, hallucinations, that sort of thing? Or is it saying that they can spend a point of Willpower to avoid the damage, giving the intruder a choice of which hit to take?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T05:37:00-08:00","id":301001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=300994#post300994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thoughts on Perilous Nest: This is an extremely powerful intrusion deterrent. When it says the attacks of the Nest can cause bashing damage, or cost a Willpower point, is that meant to represent different kinds of attacks? For damage you have poltergeists throwing stuff at intruders, or the objects in the place animate, slam doors on them, etc. Then for Willpower attacks you have horrifying hauntings, hallucinations, that sort of thing? Or is it saying that they can spend a point of Willpower to avoid the damage, giving the intruder a choice of which hit to take?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've read it as the owner of the merit decides this. So, if you do intrude - you just pay the price, without choosing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T05:42:49-08:00","id":301017,"title":"","content":"That's the way I read it as well, but it came across as slightly ambiguous. Given some of the turns the open development discussion has taken over the last few years I'm more inclined to ask rather than assume I read it correctly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T05:49:58-08:00","id":301023,"title":"","content":"After rereading it, I totally see it too. It could either be, that a nest attacks each turn, and the damage type might be decided by the ST (one turn it's WP, another it's Bashing damage), with certain Lairs having certain &quot;characters&quot; (this one mainly throws knives at you, bashing, that other one mainly terrorises you with the visions of your death - wp)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T05:52:01-08:00","id":301024,"title":"","content":"Exactly! Glad I'm not taking crazy pills. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T11:12:44-08:00","id":301312,"title":"","content":"Just wanted to state for the record that I love all of this to bits!<br /> Not a very helpful comment, I know, but it still needed to be said. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4035-lepaca","name":"Lepaca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4035_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T12:52:05-08:00","id":301437,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the ongoing feedback, folks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T17:33:04-08:00","id":301612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=300991#post300991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I originally thought the Coil of Ziva was oddly formulated as well, but I've come around after a little rumination. It's totally a combination of Anoushka's Ladder and Way of the Locust, and I think that's okay. Instead of a &quot;little goody two shoes&quot; Golconda-lite power, you retain your Humanity through force and ultimately theft. It's a brutal contradiction, and right up the Ordo Dracul's re-defined alley. You're going to keep your Beast at bay on your own terms by any means necessary, and anyone who gives you shit about it just might be next against the wall when it's time to boost the Man another notch over the Beast. Spending Vitae to guard against degeneration is fun too. Totally Coiling the curse back against itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely my intention there. Glad it was caught.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T18:56:39-08:00","id":301675,"title":"","content":"It's sorta cool how this Coil is demonstrative of the gameline's evolution in that regard, and of how Humanity has been decoupled from morality.<br /> <br /> There's also how it tangibly engages Humanity. While I don't know if that psuedo-diablerie power is gonna stay in there, I think it'd be cool to give it some narrative description that helps get what it's doing across. Am I stealing memories of being Human here? Or somehow draining them of part of how they feel human?<br /> <br /> While I was initially put off by the power, now I'm sort of fascinated by it. Despite being ostensibly heretical (I can see how it ultimately is, given the fifth dot) it's also so very like the Ordo. It's still answering the question of &quot;How do I become a better predator?&quot; but by the mastery of banes and the ability to (albeit temporarily) become human. Spooky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T19:00:42-08:00","id":301680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=300991#post300991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't think Twilight Judge needs to be &quot;toned down a lot&quot; per se, I just think it needs to be noted whether there's supposed to be one per domain as is laid out in the Ordo Dracul book, or if you can have a cadre of Twilight Judges. The merit has a ton of potential, but it gets weird if you have multiple people running around using it. It doesn't automatically make every other Dragon your bitch, you really don't have any direct sway over what they do. You can leverage them if they study, or want to study, a heretical Coil, and you have access to any Coil you want to study. It's certainly very cool, but I wouldn't say it's a problem at all. It definitely should have Sworn as a prerequisite.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am going to strongly disagree. Having a 5 dot mentor for 3xp even if just for learning coils is OP. You can leverage them for more than just coils the way the Twilight Judge merit reads. The automatic status loss is pretty OP to. There needs to be some Mechanic or repercussions for abusive Twilight Judges. Simply put the merit does way too much for the cost and has no drawbacks to balance it out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=300991#post300991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> EDIT: If in fact there can be more than one Twilight Judge, maybe a note that the higher Covenant Status Judge trumps others.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to 1E Covenant book there can be more than one Twilight Judge and it specifically says it is extremely rare for one to over turn the findings of another.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=300991#post300991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I originally thought the Coil of Ziva was oddly formulated as well, but I've come around after a little rumination. It's totally a combination of Anoushka's Ladder and Way of the Locust, and I think that's okay.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is actually bad because it goes against the theme it is trying to portray very strongly. Diablerie and Humanity do not go hand in hand as they are polar opposites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1852-maskah","name":"Maskah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T19:07:20-08:00","id":301683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maskah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=301680#post301680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is actually bad because it goes against the theme it is trying to portray very strongly. Diablerie and Humanity do not go hand in hand as they are polar opposites.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is very bad. It's existentially risky. Since you're stealing a part of somebody's self that helps keep the Beast from hollowing them out, it's the act of the desperate or the immoral. Fortunately, Humanity isn't tied to morality, so being willing to do bad things isn't actually out of character for keeping it. It IS totally in-character for <i>risking </i>it, which incidentally, the power does. It also isn't real Diablerie, so you don't eat the soul of the person involved. You take a part of them, though. You're stealing their fuel to keep your fire going. That sounds pretty Vampiric. It's the Man cannibalizing other Men to stay Human, which echoes the Kindred Condition pretty nicely.<br /> <br /> It isn't your mother's nice and goodie two shoes Anoushka's Ladder. This is a Vampire trying to keep dominion over his Beast by any means necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 11-03-2014, 10:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T20:11:48-08:00","id":301713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maskah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=301680#post301680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am going to strongly disagree. Having a 5 dot mentor for 3xp even if just for learning coils is OP. You can leverage them for more than just coils the way the Twilight Judge merit reads. The automatic status loss is pretty OP to. There needs to be some Mechanic or repercussions for abusive Twilight Judges. Simply put the merit does way too much for the cost and has no drawbacks to balance it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>5 dot Mentor effects can be cool, but since its limited to Ordo Dracul issues I don't think its problematic. Naturally in an Ordo-centric chronicle it'll be more valuable than not, but that shifting value applies to everything. As for the judgements, others only lose status if they defy your judgements, and the things you are allowed to pass judgement on are very limited. To quote the draft: &quot;She may even determine an exception to normal prohibitions of heresy within the Ordo. For example, she can rule that a character is able to learn the Coil of Ziva (see p. XX), or she might allow non-Ordo Dracul characters to develop Wyrm's Nest Merits (see below).&quot; That's it. That's what you can rule on. You can't say &quot;Give me all your shit or loose status and be murdered!&quot; If you rule that a given Dragon cannot pursue a certain Coil and they are discovered to be doing just that, <i>then</i> they lose Status.<br /> <br /> I don't buy into that every merit with a benefit needs a drawback, but if you add Sworn as a prereq, then that comes with responsibility for the Dragon to stay involved in Covenant business (and also adds another Experience to the overall cost of the merit, offsetting that arguably huge cost break for the Mentor effects). I don't think every merit representing a position of authority needs to come with a stated caveat that if you abuse your shit, people will want to oust you or get some other manner of revenge. That's just unlife in the Danse Macabre, and doesn't need to be reprinted all over the place. If you look at what this merit can actually, tangibly do, I don't think it's very abusable at all. If common sense isn't good enough to say that if a Twilight Judge blanket forbids every member of an Academy from studying Coils then she's going to have problems, I'm not sure discussion is going to get us anywhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maskah</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to 1E Covenant book there can be more than one Twilight Judge and it specifically says it is extremely rare for one to over turn the findings of another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please point out the reference you're making, because it isn't the Twilight Judge section on p. 64 of <i>Ordo Dracul</i>. If you mean this sentence: &quot;Once she has said her piece, the matter is considered resolved, and it may never again be revisited \u2014 <b>unless the Twilight Judge herself chooses to do so.</b>&quot; Emphasis mine. That pretty clearly states that nobody but <i>the</i> Twilight Judge who passed judgement can reverse it. Basically, was the merit written with the stuff in <i>Ordo Dracul</i> in mind, or not? That would go a long way to clearing this up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maskah</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is actually bad because it goes against the theme it is trying to portray very strongly. Diablerie and Humanity do not go hand in hand as they are polar opposites.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know they're opposite. That's the point. It doesn't go against the theme of retaining Humanity. It absolutely goes toward retaining Humanity, since you can suck the Humanity right out of other kindred and take it for yourself. It still risks Detachment, sure, and it builds off the Coil's lower levels that allow you to resist Detachment. It's a dark way to retain Humanity, and it doesn't come without risk. That's a very compelling power from a narrative standpoint, and the mechanics are solid. Fair enough if you don't like it, but it isn't bad.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T01:58:20-08:00","id":301944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=301713#post301713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> To quote the draft: &quot;She may even determine an exception to normal prohibitions of heresy within the Ordo. For example, she can rule that a character is able to learn the Coil of Ziva (see p. XX), or she might allow non-Ordo Dracul characters to develop Wyrm's Nest Merits (see below).&quot; That's it. That's what you can rule on. You can't say &quot;Give me all your shit or loose status and be murdered!&quot; If you rule that a given Dragon cannot pursue a certain Coil and they are discovered to be doing just that, <i>then</i> they lose Status.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's wrong. Those are just examples of what can be ruled over. Another completely fine example would be: Someone comes to Twilight Judge ( A slave for example) with an issue. (His master is abusing him, without giving him any knowledge back in return). In this example, the Twilight Judge can pass on a judgement.. and the merit kicks in. <br /> Those things you listed are just a couple of examples where he has authority. It's not &quot;That's it&quot;. There's a wide variety of issues where one can use his power (and Abuse it too).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T03:59:24-08:00","id":302014,"title":"","content":"If that's the intent then it needs to say that in the Effect section of the merit description, because it doesn't. At all. The effects are 1) 5 dot mentor relating to the Ordo, and 2) Determine exceptions to prohibition against heresy. If it also allows the Twilight Judge to trump anything said by a Status 5 Dragon then that needs to be called out explicitly. Maybe we're seeing a truncated version, but if the merit really does represent the #1 guy in an Ordo Dracul Academy it needs to state it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","user":"Smarmy Vamp","date":". 11-04-2014, 07:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T04:04:44-08:00","id":302015,"title":"","content":"Another quote from the merit: <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">&quot;a respected position trusted with rendering final judgments in internal debates.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> This one shows my point, quite explicitly. Since my example falls under &quot;internal debates&quot;. And your quote says &quot;For Example&quot;, For Example usage shows us, that it's not an exhaustive list of things, but a sub-set of a total number of possible judgments for Twilight Judge to make.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Wow, I'm using way too many words to say simple things. Anyways, to shorten it, if we're quoting stuff, let's quote all of it. My quote shows that the position (merit) is meant to judge upon much wider variety of things... Since that includes Internal Debates. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T04:05:59-08:00","id":302017,"title":"","content":"Again, then that needs to be written in the Effect section, not just the intro fluff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T04:17:38-08:00","id":302022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=302017#post302017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, then that needs to be written in the Effect section, not just the intro fluff.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So if we remove the &quot;Effect:&quot; sign everything is fine, since it's one simple text?<br /> Alright, ignoring that, let's look into Effect's section deeper:<br /> What does &quot;For Example&quot; stand for? Why it does not say: &quot;That is&quot; to show where exactly Judge's power stands? For Example clearly shows that it's not the extent of the power.<br /> Secondly in the effects, in a completely separate paragraph it says that the Judgements are sacrosanct. It does not mention that it's only the judgements of heresy.<br /> Moreover, the listing itself says &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">She may even determine an exception&quot; </span></span></span>this, once again shows that it's not only normal judgments she can make, but also judge upon heresy. That is, in addition to her normal purview (Judgments among members of the Ordo).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":294,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","user":"Griautis","date":".  Removing the reposted part. 11-04-2014, 07:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T04:19:38-08:00","id":302023,"title":"","content":"&quot;She may even determine&quot; denotes extra effects beyond the Mysteries and Mentor benefits. &quot;For example&quot; denotes the types of heresy she can adjudicate. That's all in the Effect section.<br /> <br /> I am saying that it is not clear if it's supposed to represent the stuff on Twilight Judges in the Ordo Dracul book. If that is what it's supposed to be, great! Just make sure it actually says that, which it currently doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","user":"Smarmy Vamp","date":". 11-04-2014, 07:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T04:21:06-08:00","id":302025,"title":"","content":"But scratching all that, this is not the first place where actual game effects are listed in the &quot;intro fluff&quot;, as you call it. Nor is it the last. That place is sufficient for in-game effects to be, in other powers, and in this merit as well <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Repeating this, since I edited my post after you posted further response.<br /> <br /> EDIT: It does say it. In the description of the merit, which you dismiss as &quot;intro fluff&quot;. If we dismissed all of the intro fluff, in all of the mechanical parts... we'd be dropping quite a few mechanics away <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T04:25:56-08:00","id":302027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=302025#post302025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But scratching all that, this is not the first place where actual game effects are listed in the &quot;intro fluff&quot;, as you call it. Nor is it the last. That place is sufficient for in-game effects to be, in other powers, and in this merit as well <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is a problem everywhere it occurs, not just here, and it's inconsistent. Not every game trait reveals mechanics in the description, but leaves them out of the actual mechanics writeup, and the ones that do are poorly written. If you're going to have an effect section, it needs to contain the effects of the trait.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T04:32:13-08:00","id":302029,"title":"","content":"Or not? Why can't the start contain mechanics intermixed with fluff, and then, when there's some mechanical leftovers (which can't or won't be intermixed with Fluff) that get's a space denoted as Effects, to list up this additional stuff? - It could totally be like that. Some people would hate that (I hear, some people prefer books, where Mechanics and Fluff is not intermixed at all), however it's a legit way of doing it. <br /> <br /> And in here, it's a completely legit way to go about it. Not all mechanics need to be in &quot;Effects&quot; part. Not all Fluff, needs to be &quot;Excluded&quot; from it. <br /> <br /> And, it's actually consistent. This is not the only place this is used, but it's consistent with the rest of the books, as in if the rule of writing this up is : &quot;Intro part can include some of the mechanics&quot;, then it's completely consistent with the rest of it. Maybe you don't like it, but it is. And at least I, prefer to keep it this way, instead of writing something twice - in more &quot;fluffy' part and in &quot;effects&quot; again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T04:46:41-08:00","id":302032,"title":"","content":"In point of fact, the merits in the core book are much more clearly written because <i>all</i> of their relevant text is in the effect section. If you can provide me an example of one of the other times it happens where a basic description is separate from the effect, <i>but</i> provides mechanics in the description, I'd appreciate seeing it.<br /> <br /> The closest I can find to that is discipline writeups, but as far as I can tell the mechanics are confined to the &quot;Roll Results&quot; in the case of rolled powers and the &quot;Persistent/Active&quot; effects in the case of physical disciplines.<br /> <br /> If you don't want the effect section to contain the effects of the trait, just quit dicking around and remove the effects section. All it does, if you're not going to use it, is muddy the waters and cause confusion. Things you do that cause confusion are bad. I'm not saying exclude mechanics and description. By all means make your stuff evocative, but do it <i>clearly</i>. This is not clear. If it were clear, we wouldn't be doing this right now.<br /> <br /> My bottom line is that the merits in subsequent books should follow the pattern set down in the core, because that pattern is clear. Having a giant &quot;effect&quot; section that contains most, but not all the relevant effects of the merit is madness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T04:52:05-08:00","id":302035,"title":"","content":"I did reference the disciplines mostly. <br /> Anyways, in general, I'd tend to agree with you, that having stuff clearly is good. <br /> However, in the specific case of Twilight Judge, I can say that it's fine. The effects are clear <i>enough </i>, in the merit as a whole, and in taking Effects part as it is. It's quite clear that he can make other judgements. Tho it does have it's other faults. (Which have been named in this thread before, so I won't repeat them)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T05:12:05-08:00","id":302041,"title":"","content":"Well, I'd like to see the &quot;final arbiter on any and all disputes&quot; thing nested into the effects. Other than that I like the merit as presented, and the warnings against abuse are the same kind of blanket warnings that apply to any position of power.<br /> <br /> I think having a Grandmaster/Rampant Dragon, and Parliamentarian merits would be helpful, since the Ordo Dracul is set up as an internal tripod. While they can't directly overturn a Twilight Judge's word, they can put serious pressure on her to keep her nose clean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T05:25:58-08:00","id":302045,"title":"","content":"Well, I don't think that's necessary. I trust that the Fluff side of the book (since we only see mechanics), will explore the ideas of how one becomes Twilight Judge, and how one is unmade. That way we'll know who can mess him up, and who can't. <br /> At the moment, I just think that I really miss the spot of who can unmake a Judge <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (And I don't have the Ordo Dracul book at hand, to reread that)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T05:43:35-08:00","id":302051,"title":"","content":"Oh well sure, if the OD fluff handles it, then all good.<br /> <br /> As far as who can jack with the TJ... yeah... nobody, really. There's no information on how the position is granted or revoked, and the Twilight Judge is &quot;one of two theoretically equal&quot; positions of authority within the Dying Light. The other is the Provost, but the Provost's job revolves around representing the Dying Light to the Axe and Mystery Sworn, and organizing (and chairing) the Twilight Council. The Twilight Council is pretty potent, but its still a slightly lesser version of the Twilight Judge's ability to rule on who can study what.<br /> <br /> By a direct reading of the description in the Ordo book, the TJ can only intervene and pass judgement on a dispute that is not already clearly arbitrated. So once a matter is settled, the TJ can't come in and screw with it. This behooves the Dragons to handle their squabbles internally as best they can, and only petition the Twilight Judge if they really need to, or are fairly confident that there'll be some kind of approaching-fair ruling from her.<br /> <br /> EDIT: The important bit is that most Twilight Judges just let lesser Dragons handle their own business, and only step in when it's important, or worth her time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","user":"Smarmy Vamp","date":". 11-04-2014, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T05:57:54-08:00","id":302080,"title":"","content":"Worth her time.. is such a subjective term. A politically minded Dragon will find it worth her time to interrupt most of these things... while a scientific one won't","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T06:11:15-08:00","id":302091,"title":"","content":"I just have to say that from my reading of the Merit I have to side with Griautis and this is from someone who has not read the 1st ed Requiems Ordo Dracul book. Just saying that without any baggage from previous reading the Merit seem pretty clear cut to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T06:30:07-08:00","id":302098,"title":"","content":"It is a draft so we shouldn't get too nit-picky with wording and formatting. I think everything for Twilight Judge should be moved into Effect. The &quot;description&quot; sentence really just defines the effect and then it is expanded upon later. I suggest changing &quot;specifically for&quot; to &quot;limited to&quot; so it reinforces the effective 5-dot Mentor is much more limited than the actual merit. I think &quot;limit&quot; is a better choice.<br /> <br /> The issues of multiple Judges and appeals, if possible, should be addressed someone in the book. It can't be expected for everyone to look to an older Covenant book just to figure out how to make a new Merit work. There is certainly an issue regarding whether you can &quot;shop&quot; for a judge or get a ruling overturned. With just what we have here, these issues are ambiguous. We don't know if there can be other Judges around or if a Judge normally follows some canon of law. If the Merit is the totality on the subject written in the book then a few bits of necessary info are missing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T09:06:09-08:00","id":302273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=302098#post302098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It can't be expected for everyone to look to an older Covenant book just to figure out how to make a new Merit work. There is certainly an issue regarding whether you can &quot;shop&quot; for a judge or get a ruling overturned. With just what we have here, these issues are ambiguous. We don't know if there can be other Judges around or if a Judge normally follows some canon of law. If the Merit is the totality on the subject written in the book then a few bits of necessary info are missing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very much this.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T10:21:39-08:00","id":302429,"title":"","content":"(Note: I posted some of this on the main page, but this post has some more constructive suggestions for improvement in places where I basically just wrote &quot;this is a problem&quot; before)<br /> <br /> Impaled Fighting style's wound penalty bonuses should be altered so that so that they still provide a bonus to a frenzied vampire if the vampire would normally be suffering wound penalties. This would allow for much better synergy of the fighting style with the Coil of the Wyrm mechanically. I'm also not sure why the Style has two dots of Weaponry as a pre-requisite. It's about letting other people stick sharp objects in you, not sticking them in other people! I could see a Brawler-Impaled just as easily.<br /> <br /> Shameless admission: My currently most-awaited concept is a Mystery of the Wyrm guy who uses the Rites of Impaling for chrysalis preparation, so I'd REALLY like the see the two function together mechanically. <br /> <br /> On the Wyrm's Nest Merits, I refer to the old Sidebar (p. 204, Ordo Dracul): <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Put another way, Wyrm\u2019s Nests are a part of the setting \u2014 they should always be the purview of the Storyteller, rather than a player. Even if the Storyteller gives a player a lot of say over the Nest\u2019s use in the chronicle, it belongs to the Storyteller. A Merit, as something the player buys, presents an illusion of control, and although dramatic stories can develop when Merits like Haven and Herd are threatened, the player still gets to think of them as hers. Perhaps more exactly, a Merit implies comfort, a status quo, that a Wyrm\u2019s Nest should never quite have. Wyrm\u2019s Nests shouldn\u2019t be comfortable \u2014 they should be mysterious and potentially volatile. Players should never know what to expect from a Wyrm\u2019s Nest, so the Storyteller needs to maintain possession of it.&quot; </div> </div> </div> While B&amp;S has tended towards slightly more cooperative storytelling by putting a little more narrative power in the hands of PCs, I'd still approach Wyrm's Nest merit's carefully in a few specific areas.<br /> #1: Perilous Nest should not be a Merit. Perilous Nest should be some scary **** some Nests happen to have. It should amp up the danger for Dragons, not turn it down.<br /> #2: The Nest Guardian Merit should include some further text on working to clarify the nature and type of Nest with the ST.<br /> #3: Fontal Rituals / something to do with Haunts mechanically would be cool.<br /> #4: Chapterhouse really doesn't benefit from being in the Wyrm's Nest merit list. I'd make it an independent merit, removing Nest Guardian as a pre-requisite. Flavor-wise, I think it's actually better to have the Chapterhouse itself not be a Wyrm's Nest, but rather a safe central base rather than out &quot;on the front lines&quot; like Nests are. Mechanically I like it, just alter the fluff appropriately - &quot;mystically aligned space&quot; of some kind.<br /> <br /> Siphon Soul definitely needs some work. Really like the Coil of Zirnitra. Having trouble with the Coil of Ziva but that's probably because my inner OD player is going &quot;ugh, no, heresy!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2853-wampa","name":"wampa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T10:26:30-08:00","id":302432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wampa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=302429#post302429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Siphon Soul definitely needs some work. Really like the Coil of Zirnitra. Having trouble with the Coil of Ziva but that's probably because my inner OD player is going &quot;ugh, no, heresy!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>So it's perfectly doing it's job as a heretical coil?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T10:36:21-08:00","id":302442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=302432#post302432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it's perfectly doing it's job as a heretical coil?</div> </div> </div> </div>I take every &quot;ugh, no, vampires shouldn't be doing that&quot; post as a sign that the Ordo is doing it's job. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T11:12:28-08:00","id":302462,"title":"","content":"Yes, it's doing a good job as a heretical coil.<br /> <br /> Reading it again, and seeing the logic behind it, I like Siphon the Soul. I mean, flavor-wise, it's pretty awesome. Draining the Man from others to become closer to humanity yourself? Pretty cool. Incredibly selfish, and very Ordo-like. But it may be ultimately ineffective because of the degeneration checks (and Tainted condition) it causes. The 5th dot only emphasizes the &quot;flawed premise&quot; of the Coil - it's a return to humanity, not the transcendence the Ordo seeks.<br /> <br /> All in all I like its inclusion a lot. Excited to see the 3rd-dot power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2853,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2853-wampa","user":"wampa","date":". 11-04-2014, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2853-wampa","name":"wampa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T11:52:08-08:00","id":302484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wampa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=302462#post302462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it's doing a good job as a heretical coil.<br /> <br /> Reading it again, and seeing the logic behind it, I like Siphon the Soul. I mean, flavor-wise, it's pretty awesome. Draining the Man from others to become closer to humanity yourself? Pretty cool. Incredibly selfish, and very Ordo-like. But it may be ultimately ineffective because of the degeneration checks (and Tainted condition) it causes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The degeneration check is mitigated because you can spend vitae to increase the dice rolled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T12:20:33-08:00","id":302529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=302484#post302484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The degeneration check is mitigated because you can spend vitae to increase the dice rolled.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't think about that.<br /> <br /> This Coil is officially creepy and awesome. High-humanity/BP serial diablerist...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2853,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2853-wampa","user":"wampa","date":". 11-04-2014, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2853-wampa","name":"wampa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T12:25:18-08:00","id":302531,"title":"","content":"It's not real Amaranth and keep in mind that the Vitae expenditure limitations are still in place for determining how much you can spend to help mitigate a Breaking Point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T12:40:12-08:00","id":302542,"title":"","content":"Even so, it gives your humanity vastly increased staying power if you are a &quot;real&quot; soul-muncher. Because you get a +1 hum from siphon soul, if you make the first degeneration check you can always go for full amaranth with no net loss of humanity. If you don't make the first, you still might make the second. Once you get to BP 3-4 you've got a decent shot at making 1 out of 2, which is all you need for net-humanity-neutrality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2853,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2853-wampa","user":"wampa","date":". 11-04-2014, 03:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2853-wampa","name":"wampa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T13:02:10-08:00","id":302563,"title":"","content":"Siphon Soul causes the Tainted condition, does it also cause the user to register as a Diablerist to Auspex 2? Seems likely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T13:20:18-08:00","id":302576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=302563#post302563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Siphon Soul causes the Tainted condition, does it also cause the user to register as a Diablerist to Auspex 2? Seems likely.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope so.<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>But Prince, you must realize - We Defiant only steal <b>part </b>of the soul, not the entire thing. Surely you can understand the diff... ack!</i>&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T13:21:40-08:00","id":302577,"title":"","content":"There is never a reason to not proceed to full blown soul consumption. You increase your discipline repertoire, and possibly blood potency if you do, or place yourself in a partial stage vinculum to your victim if you don't. You then cheese through the Tainted Condition by burning yourself with a lit cigarette once every couple of nights. It's a win/win for diablerie addicts. <br /> <br /> Just hope your victim doesn't decide to manifest himself in the form of a penalty to your detachment check. &gt;: )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T13:26:31-08:00","id":302602,"title":"","content":"I would never allow someone to remove Tainted Condition by burning a cigarette... that's so gamey, to border on the drawback non-existence at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T13:53:35-08:00","id":302664,"title":"","content":"That's the problem, however, with a delineated and defined path to condition removal. People will exploit it to their benefit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T14:12:32-08:00","id":302687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=302531#post302531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not real Amaranth and keep in mind that the Vitae expenditure limitations are still in place for determining how much you can spend to help mitigate a Breaking Point.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might not be, but you are stealing a part of ones soul none the less. The reality of the coil is that it is very campy with conflicting themes.<br /> <br /> I think it would be much better suited to giving you a roll with a bonus to humanity checks from Diablarie and making it harder to detect that you do that sort of thing, or maybe even be able to get rid of conditions associated with the act.<br /> <br /> Locust was evil for sure, but unlike Ziva it had a very clear theme.<br /> <br /> Ziva is a cheap cop-out to have your cake and eat it to and needs a serious re-work to have it's theme align better. It absolutely does not follow the kind of theme progression that existing B&amp;S Coils follow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1852,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1852-maskah","user":"Maskah","date":". 11-04-2014, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1852-maskah","name":"Maskah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T14:31:54-08:00","id":302694,"title":"","content":"I am curious since Twilight Judge is going to get a Merit will other status titles like Kogaian also get a Merit? I am really more in the camp that Status is the only Mechanic one should need. Titles and positions really are too fluid to be locked into a merit and really are more of an RP thing. Being sworn seems to be the only exception of this working and still being a RP thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1852-maskah","name":"Maskah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T14:48:36-08:00","id":302703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=302664#post302664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the problem, however, with a delineated and defined path to condition removal. People will exploit it to their benefit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thankfully, STs are not and have never been mindless automatons incapable of making judgement calls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T17:22:59-08:00","id":302768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maskah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=302687#post302687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It might not be, but you are stealing a part of ones soul none the less. The reality of the coil is that it is very campy with conflicting themes.<br /> <br /> I think it would be much better suited to giving you a roll with a bonus to humanity checks from Diablarie and making it harder to detect that you do that sort of thing, or maybe even be able to get rid of conditions associated with the act.<br /> <br /> Locust was evil for sure, but unlike Ziva it had a very clear theme.<br /> <br /> Ziva is a cheap cop-out to have your cake and eat it to and needs a serious re-work to have it's theme align better. It absolutely does not follow the kind of theme progression that existing B&amp;S Coils follow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it does have a pretty obvious theme progression in my view - one of forcibly clawing one's way back to humanity. The second tier involves spending blood, a symbolic representation of your damnation, to stay closer to humanity. The 4th tier involves forcing others closer to the Beast so you can become closer to the Man. The 5th is a brief return to the Man.<br /> <br /> The potential problem is a character abusing the mechanical benefits of the Coil to go on sprees of rampant diablerie (or other particularly villainous acts) while using the 2nd and 4th tiers to stop his humanity from falling significantly. The easiest way to discourage this would be to cap Buttress the Soul at doubling the -base- dice pool (per p.107 of B&amp;S) and make Siphon the Soul a Humanity 2 detachment roll. This would mean Buttress the Soul wouldn't help you if you were committing mass murder or drinking people's souls, but would help you a lot with having selfish thoughts.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2853-wampa","name":"wampa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T17:36:14-08:00","id":302782,"title":"","content":"I'd allow them to burn themselves with a cigarette.<br /> <br /> After all, Kindred are <i>really</i> flammable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T21:58:02-08:00","id":302978,"title":"","content":"A question about the Coil of Zirnitra and the Thief of Fate merit:<br /> <br /> Would you have to spend 1wp + 1 Vitae to prevent yourself from stealing someone's luck?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T22:03:10-08:00","id":302983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=302442#post302442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I take every &quot;ugh, no, vampires shouldn't be doing that&quot; post as a sign that the Ordo is doing it's job. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to agree, especially if we are talking IC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T07:19:23-08:00","id":303256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=302703#post302703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thankfully, STs are not and have never been mindless automatons incapable of making judgement calls.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true, but when the mechanics support an argument, it is much more difficult to rationalize a change. Glad I don't really have that problem (no 2nd Edition for me). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T07:32:11-08:00","id":303262,"title":"","content":"More difficult? No, it's not at all. You just say &quot;I'm making this change, because it's ridiculous and is power gaming.&quot;. And you're done. If you have such a power gamer player, then you have a different problem <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T07:51:04-08:00","id":303270,"title":"","content":"Which works fine, if your game is contained and you are the only one GM'ing. When that is not the case, it is always better to stay as close to the Book rules as you can, rather than everyone having potentially different houserules. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T08:02:05-08:00","id":303290,"title":"","content":"Which is still a small issue, if the GMs can agree to specific house rules <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> for example, scratching that part off the Condition whatsoever. I really find hard time conjuring scenarios were that would feel appropriate <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Speaking of which, perhaps I'll create a thread specifically to discuss Tainted condition. (if there's none already)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T11:14:07-08:00","id":304743,"title":"","content":"Couldn't the new crucible rituals actually be scales? If you think about the ritualistic nature of scales crucible rituals fit in very nicely. In fact it would actually make sense to have a Coil that invovlves manipulating and/or benefiting from these energies for which these coils fall under. One of the benefits could be that an individual can replenish their vitae on a 1 for 1 basis (ignoring feeding restrictions) by feeding on the energies from the site.<br /> <br /> Spoiling was mentioned earlier in this thread and I believe it can be handled in the same manner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1852-maskah","name":"Maskah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T10:21:12-08:00","id":305887,"title":"","content":"Why is the Coil of \u017diva banned? The Ordo is all about research, and you know what's really bad for research? Degenerating in to animalistic madness. How many peer reviewed papers on the vampiric condition do you think Draugr produce?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T10:23:52-08:00","id":305889,"title":"","content":"I'd venture it's because the Coil primarily focuses on running away from the beast by means of mauling and degenerating other vampires. It'd have to be banned for PR reasons if not for purely philosophical ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T10:34:00-08:00","id":305924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=305889#post305889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd venture it's because the Coil primarily focuses on running away from the beast by means of mauling and degenerating other vampires. It'd have to be banned for PR reasons if not for purely philosophical ones.</div> </div> </div> </div> Of the 4 coils and 1 scale we can see, only the 4th level coil involves &quot;mauling and degenerating other vampires&quot;. I wouldn't call 20% of something it's &quot;primarily focus&quot;.<br /> <br /> And the scale &quot;bleed the sin&quot; can actually help other vampires. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T10:50:50-08:00","id":305934,"title":"","content":"Anyone aspiring to the Coil of Ziva is inevitably aspiring towards that 4th dot, and even if 90% of aspirants don't reach it the objective itself remains threatening.<br /> <br /> However, more than that the Coil stands opposed to most of the Ordo on a philosophical level. It's a retreat from the Beast, a gradual softening towards being human again. The Ordo is a massively hypocritical group, each aspiring to their own version of heresy while decrying the paths of others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T10:52:39-08:00","id":305937,"title":"","content":"It's banned because it isn't progress, it's regression. The point of the Ordo Dracul is to transcend the curse of vampirism into something <i>more</i>, something <i>better</i>. Not to regress to the weakness and fragile impermanence of mortality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T11:37:27-08:00","id":306002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=305937#post305937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's banned because it isn't progress, it's regression. The point of the Ordo Dracul is to transcend the curse of vampirism into something <i>more</i>, something <i>better</i>. Not to regress to the weakness and fragile impermanence of mortality.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah and turning into a Draugr is so much <i>more</i>, so much <i>better</i> isn't it?<br /> <br /> The Coil of Ziva allows you to retain your mind while acting beyond good and evil, in that sense you're becoming super-vampire","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T11:42:27-08:00","id":306009,"title":"","content":"Because that's only a sub-set of the Coil, and points like this are why Twilight Judges grant exceptions to heresy. Ultimately this Coil pushes you away from being a vampire and toward being mortal. That is the ultimate expression of the Mystery, completely shedding all things vampiric and being mortal again. Snark about it all you like, I suppose, but that's why it's proscribed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T11:44:58-08:00","id":306012,"title":"","content":"That there's arguments both for and against it as a heresy are why its controversial and part of the flavor. One Dragon might argue the ultimate predator is the one who can overcome and deny his Beast utterly, while another will call that an absurd twisting of Dragon doctrine.<br /> <br /> If you're gonna play a character who follows that mystery (A Zivite? I hope there's a cool word in there somewhere...) than it'll be prudent to ask yourself what their stance is, how they might defend it, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T11:47:25-08:00","id":306014,"title":"","content":"Turning into a Draugr would be considered a failure, especially for the Path of the Wyrm. They're about weaponizing the Beast, not succumbing to it, they just haven't quite perfected the Coil yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T11:47:59-08:00","id":306015,"title":"","content":"I'd go with Zivan.<br /> <br /> I can absolutely see a Twilight Judge granting clemency to a Dragon who wants to study the first few Coils of Ziva, but ruling that Shedding the Beast's Skin is out of bounds. I can likewise see the attitude existing that even taking a few steps on that twisting path are too much temptation, and ultimately lead to perversion of the Ordo's Great Work. Schism, baby! Good, and good for you. Or for your games, at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T11:52:39-08:00","id":306019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=306009#post306009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because that's only a sub-set of the Coil,</div> </div> </div> </div> It's 4/5 of what we can see. That's a large sub-set.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=306009#post306009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ultimately this Coil pushes you away from being a vampire and toward being mortal. That is the ultimate expression of the Mystery, completely shedding all things vampiric and being mortal again.</div> </div> </div> </div> 1/5 of what we can see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T11:56:21-08:00","id":306021,"title":"","content":"That's probably how the Mystery made it so far while it was being created. It looked great, right up until the ultimate expression of the Coil, then all the mainstream Defiant jump back and say, &quot;Whoa, what the fuck?&quot; From there its an easy leap to see the entire thing being branded as heresy and stamped out, but for tiny pockets and resurgence here and there over the years.<br /> <br /> All kinds of basically good ideas get crushed because of opposition from those in power who don't like the implications of the ideas. Galileo can offer a word or two of advice on the subject.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also bear in mind we haven't seen the 3rd dot yet. If it's more Locust-y, then it might make even more sense why it's banned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T11:57:54-08:00","id":306023,"title":"","content":"Coils can't be viewed through their constituent bits, dots are just the mechanical representation of a greater pilgrimage. The fundamental objective of Ziva is to attain &quot;humanity&quot;, in this case it is to become human and free of the Beast. <br /> <br /> That said, everyone should remember that this is a draft and an incomplete one at that. It may well be subject to change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T17:58:03-08:00","id":306290,"title":"","content":"The Coil of Ziva says the Dragon rejects the things that make her a vampire and clings hard to Humanity as the reason the Ordo Dracul considers the Coil heretical. I think that is a clear and reasonable explanation. Dots 1, 2, and 4 would be very attractive to Dragons. They don't object to Diablerie, as long as the victim is an outsider and you don't get caught. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I also doubt they mind munching and degenerating other vampires, again, as long as the &quot;others&quot; are outsiders. One of the common Coils suggests other vampires would not appreciate experiments dealing with that Coil. Dragons obviously do some truly evil shit at times. They respect the traditions amongst themselves and consider them an often necessary evil regarding outsiders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T19:04:00-07:00","id":488950,"title":"","content":"*casts threadnecromatic ressucitation*<br /> <br /> *hides for cover*<br /> <br /> It's ALIVE!<br /> --<br /> <br /> Ok, since this is still technically in Open Development, and therefore still open for questions and feedbacks, I'm guessing this is not a breach of netiquette.<br /> --<br /> <br /> About the Coil of \u017diva:<br /> <br /> First off, I love it. Denying the Bane and Buttress the Soul are amazing, and so is Bleed the Skin. Funny thing is that, unless you are willing to run away from the Ordo Dracul the rest of your unlife, you basically need Twilight Judge and Status: Ordo Dracul at three dots each. Which is a pretty steep requirement from the get go.<br /> <br /> <b>Denying the Bane</b>, as mentioned earlier in the thread, would benefit from being clearer, with examples of sort. Does it apply to Torpor duration and Sunlight damage on the charts? How does it apply to the different clan Banes (do you substract the Mekhet's -1 from Humanity for banes like Sunlight and then add +X afterwards? Does this mean you can end up... with a negative penalty, thus a bonus (I'm stretching it on purpose here), or does the effect already apply to Torpor duration and Sunlight damage, etc.). This would be a very powerful Coil, and synergize with Coil of the Ascendant very much, but I think it would be balanced by the fact you just paid 6 Experiences for Twilight Judge and its prerequisites in order to avoid a blood hunt against ya.<br /> <br /> <b>Buttress the Soul</b>, on the other hand, seems 100% clear. The temptation of spending too much blood is inevitably going to trigger breaking points to regain said blood, which is interesting narratively. This is an interesting gamble. Though if you already have multiple touchstone and really chug through vitae like crazy, this could lead to almost guaranteed successes on Detachment rolls, and tons of Beats because of high humanity. Something the Storyteller needs to watch out for.<br /> <br /> (table shows the % chance of failing a Detachment roll) <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">8d---</td> <td align=\"right\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">5,76%</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">9d---</td> <td align=\"right\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">4,04%</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">10d--</td> <td align=\"right\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">2,82%</td> </tr> </table></div> <b>Bleed the Skin:</b> if you can apply this on yourself, this can be interesting. (Can it be applied on one self?) Let's say you stay at crazy high Humanity, you keep having to roll for Detachment <i>for so many little things</i>, and gain tons of Beats. If you fail, simply purchase Humanity back at discount, and keep getting Beats coming. This could be abused by a smart and subtle player, something to watch out for.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, the cost of entry in all of this is still pretty steep, but I can see how it could be mechanically employed by a clever player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T02:17:02-07:00","id":489183,"title":"","content":"Wow, how did I miss this?<br /> <br /> Umm...I'm not going to be much help as I don't know what to do to fix it but...aside from the few Scales and the Coil allowing me to buy up stuff like Telekinesis or interact with Spirits/Ghosts/etc. (which is only cool because of the other things it lets you buy) nothing here interests me.<br /> <br /> I wanted more mad science, more occult psuedoscience channeled through the curse, more...<i>things that I do, actions that I take</i> which the Scales give directly. You can only use a Scale by going out and doing something gruesomely scientific while the Coils/Merits...feel less like that.<br /> <br /> The merits do nothing for me. As of right now I wouldn't take any of them. The Wyrm Nest ones seem like a potentially very large investment for a game in which I suspect very little time would be spent within them.<br /> <br /> Though I do query if the wolf-blooded thing is allowed could you get access to the upgraded Sleepwalker merit that is in the Silver Ladder book that allows you to buy Mage Rotes for merit dots? 'Cos we all want to see time bending vampires like the spell that allows you to completely reqrite your own history and respend all your XP. Or perhaps Life/Space to apport blood from someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","user":"Scutarii","date":". 04-23-2015, 05:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T03:33:41-07:00","id":489199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=489183#post489183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Though I do query if the wolf-blooded thing is allowed could you get access to the upgraded Sleepwalker merit that is in the Silver Ladder book that allows you to buy Mage Rotes for merit dots? 'Cos we all want to see time bending vampires like the spell that allows you to completely reqrite your own history and respend all your XP. Or perhaps Life/Space to apport blood from someone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I probably wouldn't let players buy first edition material in a second edition game. But, discretion is wise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T05:48:41-07:00","id":489398,"title":"","content":"Actually thinking about it more...I think my issue is something I've been noticing more as VtR2e has gone (it may have been prevalent in 1e as well but I barely played 1e). There are a lot of merits that interact with other passive merits. Such as Herd, Feeding Ground, Notary, Twilight Judge, etc. A lot of these probably come up as very specific applications of broader merits like Status or Contacts or come up as relevant for a single plot but they don't let my character do something new and cool.<br /> <br /> Let's say I am a Notary. More people pay attention to me, I can trade a new kind of favour, I have some more clout and importance in the political game, so it definitely has value but I don't <i>do</i> much with it that is unique to it. Having a high Status would give me a similar <i>kind</i> of approach to things, even if the specifics were different.<br /> <br /> Similarly with the Wyrms Nest. Ok, my character has a nest and their Haven and Safe Place are linked to it an surrounded with a Feeding Ground. I now have what amounts to a well protected home base of operations. I can trade some other new types of favours so again, has value. But I'm not <i>really</i> doing anything new when I have them. Day to day I;m still going to Elysiums or protecting my turf from invaders or hijacking the procurement department of a museum.<br /> <br /> I like the Dracul as they are represented in some ways as a group that politics less and <i>does</i> things more. They go out and <i>do</i> monstrous things for 'science'. The Lance sacrifice sacraments but those are often not too onerous to get ahold of. The Crone spend blood for their unique thing and the default state of vampires is acquiring blood. The Carthians and Invictus play the politics game that I wanted t move away from. The Dracul however go out and create vile concotions of blood, salt and rendered human fat and force others to drink it and vomit out their vinculum. It's that side of them that appeals to me.<br /> <br /> This particular set of stuff feels less like it plays up the aspects of the Dracul that made me want to play as one.<br /> <br /> Starting a session with an Aspiration of 'find a victim to peel off their skin to scrape off the fat layer underneath' feels distinctly unique to a Dracul character while an Aspiration of 'bribe James with access to my nest to get him to overlook Monica's indiscretions' feels like it could slot into any of the Covenants, just swap Nest for Notary or Safe Place or Herd or Feeding Ground or...etc.<br /> <br /> I now that these kinds of merits are needed for verisimilitude, for world building and for those players who do enjoy that kind of game play so I in no way would want to see them removed. I just want to see more Flesh Grafting, more reasons why I would want to reenact the scene from the core book with the kindred strapped to a table with their flesh peeled back to expose their rib cage. Give me Scales and Coils that require me to engage in some form of activity/experiment/physical thing to use them.<br /> <br /> Sigh. I know this isn't particularly useful, I'm basically saying to give me less of the stuff I don't like and more of the stuff I do like and also rather late into the process as this went up in 2014!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","user":"Scutarii","date":". 04-23-2015, 08:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T06:27:23-07:00","id":489416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=489398#post489398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's say I am a Notary. More people pay attention to me, I can trade a new kind of favour, I have some more clout and importance in the political game, so it definitely has value but I don't <i>do</i> much with it that is unique to it. Having a high Status would give me a similar <i>kind</i> of approach to things, even if the specifics were different.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, there's a bit more of a difference than that. Notaries are required to be present for the use of any Oath to take effect.<br /> <br /> A notary can make personal oaths with no one else present. While the core book oaths are often between a liege and follower, there's a number of the new ones that can be made in a vacuum if you have the Notory merit. For instance, they could swear the Oath of the True Knight at will to avoid being forcefully blood bonded. Oath of the Refugee for a nomadic cotorie establishing safety. In theory, the GM could allow a spontaneous new Oath to take place as well. <br /> <br /> A lot of the things you can do with these merits aren't always obvious at first glance. Chapter House, for instance. If you're a Majesty or Nightmare user, you'd love it for making it less likely for someone to resist your powers. Having what amounts to a highly effective Elysium where your powers are uncontested is pretty nice.<br /> <br /> Many mortal supernatural powers use skill rolls (usually an Occult roll). Adding in your Occult Alignment dots could be helpful when you're investing in the Coil of Ziva.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T11:04:46-07:00","id":489656,"title":"","content":"Are we ever going to playtest the 3rd tier of the Coil of \u017diva?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T17:30:50-07:00","id":490080,"title":"","content":"Siphon the Soul as is would let me drain 3 low humanity BP1s and reach humanity 10 I think. If so you might want to look into making it need a higher humanity vic<span style=\"font-size:12px\">tim/changing how long tainted lasts. A<span style=\"font-family:arial\">lso <span style=\"color:#000000\">Crucible </span></span></span>feels like it belongs in 1e, lower xp costs isn't something 2e does much.<br /> I want a Scale for sheading the beasts skin that can turn a revenant back to human.<br /> and as others have said Judge should need you to be sworn.<br /> Other than that I have no problem with this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T04:24:00-07:00","id":656343,"title":"","content":"THE UNDEAD RISE AGAIN!<br /> <br /> Sorry for necroing this, I just made some alterations to \u017diva, thought you guys might like it:<br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Soul of Life </b></span>\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">This coil allows the vampire to fool both herself and her beast with the mimicry of life. Upon learning this coil, the vampire chooses a virtue, a vice, and a ritual exclusive to mortals (such as a family dinner, drunken partying, etc.). So long as she benefits from the blush of life, she has the chosen virtue, vice, and ritual, in addition to her mask and dirge. The ritual takes at least an hour to complete, restores a point of Willpower, but can only be performed once each night.</span></b><br /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Denying the Hold </b></span>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Dragons that have mastered this coil can deny the hold of the Beast over the Man through sheer tenacity. When subjected to a condition uniquely experienced by Kindred, such as Jaded, Tempted, or Competitive, she can spend a point of Willpower to attempt a Resolve + Composure + Coil roll. On a success, the condition is not applied at all. On an exceptional success, the condition is not applied, and the next time she is subjected to the same condition, she needn't spend Willpower to reject it.</span></b><br /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Shedding the Beast's Skin</b> </span>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">The final spiral in \u017diva\u2019s Coil has the Dragon literally shed her flesh, and with it, her vampiric nature. She spends three Willpower and three Vitae to activate Shedding the Beast\u2019s Skin. Shedding the skin takes five turns. Shedding the Beast\u2019s Skin lasts for twelve hours, minus one for each dot of the Dragon\u2019s Blood Potency. During this time, she becomes effectively human. Her heart beats. Her skin sweats. She can get hungry, and she can eat. She can engage in sexual activity as if human. She easily passes medical scrutiny. She can walk out into the sun. This comes with it a loss of her vampiric advantages (except for those granted by this mystery; she retains the virtue, vice, and ritual granted by Soul of Life), Disciplines, her ability to ingest, store, and expend Vitae, and her immortality. She no longer suffers any vampiric bane, has no predatory aura, and does not experience blood sympathy. At the end of the period, she becomes Kindred again. For nearly a half an hour, she undergoes the sensations and transformations of the Embrace again. This leaves her functionally incapacitated during this time. She can hold off the transformation for one minute for an additional point of Willpower. During this transformation, her Vitae drops to 0, possibly causing a hunger frenzy. She immediately takes damage from any exposure to the sun as if her Blood Potency was 1 and Humanity was 7, and she vomits all food and drink consumed during her time as a mortal, possibly causing an anger frenzy. At the end of the transformation, she takes aggravated damage equal to her Blood Potency, possibly causing a fear frenzy. This damage leaves no scars. After all is said and done, the vampire regains all spent Willpower, and gains the Inspired condition.</span></b><br /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Bleed the Sin</b><br /> Prerequisite Coil: Buttress the Soul \u2022\u2022</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Procedure: With this procedure, the Dragon bleeds a subject of all their blood or Vitae. With human subjects, this generally requires a dialysis machine or other technological assistance to keep the subject alive. This flow of blood carries with it the weight of their sin. Outcome: The subject must remain effectively bloodless for at least ten minutes in order for this Scale to take effect. Reduce the subject\u2019s next Humanity, Integrity, or similar trait purchase by one Experience per dot of the vampire\u2019s Coil of \u017diva.</span></b><br /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Siphon the Soul</b><br /> Prerequisite Coil: Denying the Hold \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">This ability acts as a sort of pseudo-Amaranth. The vampire drains a victim completely, then continues to do so further. She spends Willpower and rolls Composure + Resolve (instead of the Strength + Resolve called for normally, see Vampire: The Requiem, p. 101). On a success, add the successes of that roll to the victim's Humanity or Integrity. If this exceeds the vampire's Humanity, she steals one dot of Humanity from her victim. He loses it\u037e she gains one. She may only ever strip one such dot from a given victim. A mortal victim drained this way falls into a coma and takes the vampire's Blood Potency as aggravated damage. A vampire victim only reaches torpor as result of this. Regardless, the attacker suffers Detachment at Humanity 1 (possibly losing the stolen Humanity dot), and suffers the Tainted Condition (with Blood Potency as 1 for mortals). This act can be extended into a full Amaranth.</span></b><br /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T05:19:10-07:00","id":656399,"title":"","content":"I think you may have gone a bit overboard with the downsides of Shedding the Beast's Skin. I mean, what sort of dragon would consider a coil that can easily kill the user a finished product?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T23:19:43-07:00","id":657428,"title":"","content":"You think so? It is possible... however, spending a day as a mortal is still a big deal, so... not sure how I'd balance it out without some dramatic cost to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T02:44:02-07:00","id":657571,"title":"","content":"If you spend an entire <i>day </i>as a mortal then as written you'll get about 60 lethal in sun damage and immediately die when it wears off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T04:20:21-07:00","id":657635,"title":"","content":"Only if you spend the whole day sunbathing...<br /> I was thinking of limiting that particular damage to max out at your health -1 aggravated, but I fear the write-up could be complicated. You'd axe the sun damage entirely?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T05:49:26-07:00","id":657749,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what I'd cut, but I think losing all vitae, vomiting up everything you ate, taking a bunch of lethal damage, taking a bunch of aggravated damage <i>and </i>frenzying three times is a bit much.<br /> <br /> And then after all that you have this vampire lying in a pool of barf going &quot;wow, I feel so inspired right now.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T03:18:57-07:00","id":659176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=489199#post489199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I probably wouldn't let players buy first edition material in a second edition game. But, discretion is wise.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well first edition proximi can't be embraced, so I think to it's safe to say one can disallow that without making any generalizations anyway. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T14:44:08-08:00","id":817972,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I was thinking. What would happen to a vampire with Coil of Zirnitra and City-walk who use the merit to city walk from city to city and never see the sunlight? Vampires can be tired after 24 hours of night? Same question for north pole nights, some nights can last for months.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":7210,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","user":"Horodrigo","date":". 01-27-2016, 05:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T15:09:53-08:00","id":817990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=817972#post817972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. I was thinking. What would happen to a vampire with Coil of Zirnitra and City-walk who use the merit to city walk from city to city and never see the sunlight? Vampires can be tired after 24 hours of night? Same question for north pole nights, some nights can last for months.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would not have them suffer the draw of Daysleep, but still have them pay Vitae each night to stay animated. Perhaps even make it 2 Vitae per day in the long run as they need more &quot;force&quot; to stay animated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T16:37:28-08:00","id":818044,"title":"","content":"No real rules for that, because, lets be honest, what vampire is going to do that? In theory, you could do the same thing with a jet. Three major drives of vampires include 1) avoid dying 2) avoid being bored and 3) get blood. 1 is harder but doable. 2 and 3 get to be an issue fast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T17:01:22-08:00","id":818062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=817990#post817990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would not have them suffer the draw of Daysleep, but still have them pay Vitae each night to stay animated.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would be my ruling as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T17:20:44-08:00","id":818078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=818044#post818044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No real rules for that, because, lets be honest, what vampire is going to do that? In theory, you could do the same thing with a jet. Three major drives of vampires include 1) avoid dying 2) avoid being bored and 3) get blood. 1 is harder but doable. 2 and 3 get to be an issue fast.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... you'd get bored <i>faster</i> if you went globetrotting?<br /> <br /> It would make a fun NPC - a Vampire messenger who ferries packages and messages between Princes and Vampires. Multiple cities have given him small feeding grounds to cover his &quot;costs&quot;. He insists on wearing leather jackets and aviators.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T17:45:50-08:00","id":818092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=818078#post818078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So... you'd get bored <i>faster</i> if you went globetrotting?<br /> <br /> It would make a fun NPC - a Vampire messenger who ferries packages and messages between Princes and Vampires. Multiple cities have given him small feeding grounds to cover his &quot;costs&quot;. He insists on wearing leather jackets and aviators.</div> </div> </div> </div> I had a similar thought about a child of the thorns, after all being able to travel from mirror to mirror anywhere in the world certainly beats traveling coach, and if they wanted why they could just set up a system to live double lives, across the globe from each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T18:09:00-08:00","id":818106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=818078#post818078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... you'd get bored <i>faster</i> if you went globetrotting?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, because you'd be constantly on the move. You'd never be able to just sit back and relax, because you'd always be on a time table. Add that to the fact that the overwhelming majority of things that people want to see and do while globe trotting? Tend to be open during the day, which defeats the whole purpose of this mental exercise. Sunlight is a thematic thing in VtR, not because its a way to physically injure vampires, but because its a restriction on being able to interact fully with humans during normal business hours. <br /> <br /> Jumping between two or three cities would probably be more stable; my first thought was a more nomadic life style. Now, the original question has some bearing when you're set in Alaska. Which, in all honestly, is a huge change - people there have to be nocturnal for half the year! It has other thematic issues; as I mentioned, business hours with sunlight is a thing. In no-sunrise for long periods of time, there's business hours at night, which is different. I'd probably make the vamps active without penalty, but then sporadic in rising, because OMG sunlight for days without night will force torpor on pretty much everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T18:39:33-08:00","id":818118,"title":"","content":"Did anyone get around to playtesting this or the other open development spoilers in their games? My vampire game ended like right before the Open Dev's started, so I didn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T06:46:04-08:00","id":842529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=818118#post818118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did anyone get around to playtesting this or the other open development spoilers in their games? My vampire game ended like right before the Open Dev's started, so I didn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm testing this material in a crossover &quot;Vampire x Changeling&quot;.<br /> Zirnitra quickly became the favorite Coil of the coterie. They have developed some scales in contact with the changelings.<br /> Some members are starting a cult between fae-touched, changelings, ghouls and vampires.<br /> <br /> The points that I'd like to adress are:<br /> 1. Perilous Nest merit is too strong. Damage or Willpower loss <b>every turn</b> can make some hard traps. I have changed it to calculate the damage over the course of 10 minutes. <br /> 2. Grafting Unholy Flesh needs some clarification. In both Procedure and Outcome.<br /> 2.1 The procedure: If the body part is something that you already have(like a hand), you replace one of your hands, or now you have 3 hands? And wich kind of powers can you stole with this? Innate abilities? Only exp cost powers? You get them for free?<br /> 2.2 The outcome: Can you heal the stolen body part with vitae? Or once it had taken some damage, you need to be extra careful to not lose it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T13:58:05-07:00","id":883189,"title":"","content":"I've arrived late to this thread, and if this has been addressed I apologize.<br /> <br /> Regarding the Coil of Ziva, what if the Ordo is getting it wrong (or, what if the real reason it's heretical is because it allows you to become like the Brood)? If the idea is to transcend the vampiric condition, this Coil allows exactly that: transcend the limits humanity (Humanity) imposes on a vampire. If Banes include sunlight damage and Torpor (I don't see why not), you make the third dot lessen the social penalty for interacting with humans and boom! Now you have a kindred that is quite functional at Humanity 2 or 1 but with no moral qualms getting in the way of his quest to become whatever.<br /> <br /> When I started looking at the Coil as 'how do I mitigate the effects my dwindling Humanity causes to my condition' and not 'how do I become more human', fourth level made total sense. The fifth level makes sense from a 'spitting in the eye of God' manner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11149,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11149-pj123","user":"PJ123","date":". 05-05-2016, 05:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11149-pj123","name":"PJ123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T06:55:17-07:00","id":883713,"title":"","content":"Thats pretty GrimDark, I think... give<br /> <br /> <br /> one thing, how difficult is it to find a Teacher for the coil, assuming the DEFAULT understanding, not PJ123s, charming fan theory.<br /> <br /> I think its believable for its practicioners, to be part of the mainstream body of the ordodracul, in 2 or 3 towns, given the insular nature of Requiem vampiric politics. ir a ST wants to slacken things up a LITTLE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T07:42:10-07:00","id":883764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PJ123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/292532-open-development-ordo-dracul-merits-and-mysteries?p=883189#post883189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the Coil of Ziva, what if the Ordo is getting it wrong (or, what if the real reason it's heretical is because it allows you to become like the Brood)? If the idea is to transcend the vampiric condition, this Coil allows exactly that: transcend the limits humanity (Humanity) imposes on a vampire. If Banes include sunlight damage and Torpor (I don't see why not), you make the third dot lessen the social penalty for interacting with humans and boom! Now you have a kindred that is quite functional at Humanity 2 or 1 but with no moral qualms getting in the way of his quest to become whatever.<br /> <br /> When I started looking at the Coil as 'how do I mitigate the effects my dwindling Humanity causes to my condition' and not 'how do I become more human', fourth level made total sense. The fifth level makes sense from a 'spitting in the eye of God' manner.</div> </div> </div> </div> Becoming human again is an absolute heresy to the Ordo Dracul, whereas transcending penalties and becoming more of a monster, even a lich-like one that devours souls, is not. <br /> <br /> Ziva seems to be a mix of the old Coils of the Ladder, and Coils of the Locust, so it could swing either way, saint or sinner. So, you're right, but the opposite is correct as well, I think. It all depends on what the final product ends up being. We're still missing a dot, and this was only a playtest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}